{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys","id":1244941,"title":"Are the Dragon Blooded the good guys?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-11T15:33:04-07:00","id":1244941,"title":"Are the Dragon Blooded the good guys?","content":"First off, I want to say that I usually hate these kind of posts. Like arguments where the technocracy are the good guys etc. However. I have been running Exalted 3e for about 8 months now with no experience in earlier editions except a few supplements I picked up to assist my game. As my players are currently pursuing a way to prevent the loom of fate from tracking them, its brought up a lot of existential questions about the usurpation. From my perspective, it seems as if the sidereals and dbs were probably right to put down the solars. The great curse seems like an incredible threat to creation. Sure things havn't been perfect since that time, but having a bunch of insane solars and lunars be better? My players think the great curse is a lie because they are clearly the good guys. I want to present my story from that perspective since my characters are solars, but I am having a hard time making sense of it in my own head. How is the return of solars a good thing? Is it the only way to stop a variety of other threats to creation the dragon blooded can't handle? What am I missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T15:50:37-07:00","id":1244949,"title":"","content":"Assuming that you mean the Realm, no. It's an oppressive empire out to plunder wealth from the rest of the world so that it can continue to have sick-ass parties in palatial estates. Lunars and Solars, meanwhile, often come from backgrounds at the other end of the wealth and privilege spectrum. Hence, the Lunars and Solars would be punching upward. Dynasts that want to keep the status quo to enjoy sick parties, slaves, and manorial households are part of the problem; Dynasts who want to abolish slavery, enact political reform, and curtail cruelty, though, might be on to something, even if they are likely to be painfully out of touch most of the time. Also, the latter are a minority who might only get most of what they want by allying with other powers... like, say, Lunars and Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T16:00:34-07:00","id":1244955,"title":"","content":"It depends on your perspective. IMHO, Exalted has generally come down on the side of &quot;It was a justifiable decision, inasmuch as uprising, bloody revolution, and causing the end of an Age could be justified. But whether it was 'right'...we'll never tell. We don't know.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T16:08:09-07:00","id":1244960,"title":"","content":"It is my estimation that <b>any Exalt type is permitted to be &quot;the good guys&quot; of a given narrative or story</b>. The Solars will be the heroes in a Solar story and the mad tyrannical returning god-kings in a DB story.<br /> The Solars and Lunars have great power to change the world and oppose forces that would cause harm to those less empowered.<br /> The Sidereals work tirelessly to keep Creation moving towards what they may hope is a better future, capable of weaving fates to improve lives.<br /> The Dragon-Blooded can fight to defend those below them as well even if they lack the personal might to go toe-to-toe with some of the things other Exalted fight.<br /> Even Abyssals can try to improve the lives and well-being of both the living and the dead, acting as a peaceful mediator to ensure prosperity of both underworld and the living.<br /> <br /> <b>And at the same time, no Exalt type is universally The Good Guys:</b><br /> Solars have a severe propensity towards being egomaniacs who will flip all the tables and upend every system to get what they want.<br /> Lunars have been raging and tearing at the edges of the world, waging a scorched earth campaign against every outpost and bastion of the Realm.<br /> The Sidereals often make the hard choice of triage and acceptable losses; Romeo and Juliet committing suicide is an acceptable cost to end the unending turmoil between Montague and Capulet.<br /> And Abyssals can be rampaging monsters spreading misery and decay to force people to pay obeisance to the dead.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded of the Realm, admittedly, have a much harder time being called undeniably 'good', not because of any Inherent Cosmological Principle of Evil, but because as scions of the Realm they are beneficiaries and executors of a brutal tribute-taking engine aiming to extract resources from the threshold to grant luxury and opulence to the center.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T16:23:34-07:00","id":1244965,"title":"","content":"as Meianno said, it's entirely, 100% possible for you to say the Usurpation is good and that the Realm, specifically, is bad.<br /> <br /> No one is made evil by their Exaltation (as far as we know anyway), people are people, and power may corrupt or may not.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of ways to resolve such a feeling, but one thing I am curious about; do the PCs not think the Great Curse, or do the Players? the Players should know the great curse exists since they track limit. But the Solars are certainly justified in feeling like they were betrayed and nothing is wrong with them, even as they begin limit breaking.<br /> <br /> if you're interested in asking this question, I think it depends on how you want to do it; maybe the DBs were right, but that doesn't mean the Realm is right to imperialize the world. Maybe the Solars find out the Great Curse IS real, and they have to realize that they were justified, and they have to deal with the Curse and what that means.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Solars don't think about it this way, and killing the Solars was wrong; they're justified in thinking this, and maybe they're right, or maybe they're wrong, depending on how you want to make the story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T16:48:30-07:00","id":1244970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1244949#post1244949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that you mean the Realm, no. It's an oppressive empire out to plunder wealth from the rest of the world so that it can continue to have sick-ass parties in palatial estates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wellll\u2026.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoff Grabowski</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The Realm is a giant machine for raping all the jade out of the world and letting 10,000 people live as god-kings in golden palaces at someone else's expense, and it bends social, poilitical, religious and military force to that end. The Realm also guards the world against the armies of the Fair Folk and the Lunar Anathema and provides some sort of rudimentary check against total anarchy in the Threshold. It uses social, political, military and religious force to do that too. Good and evil don't enter into it. </span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Certainly, avoid the narrative where the latter means that the former is straightforwardly justified, but it is a bit more nuanced.<br /> <br /> Now more than ever, I think, with things like House Ledaal and how much they're concerned by those Deathlords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T17:18:02-07:00","id":1244983,"title":"","content":"Of course they were, the Immaculate doctrine makes clear that they are the rightful rulers of this world and any gold or silver asshole who might say otherwise is a body snatching demon.<br /> <br /> The real question we should ask is whether Lookshy's refusal to bend knee to the Empress despite not being possessed by demons makes them DOUBLE evil, or merely misguided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T17:56:05-07:00","id":1244995,"title":"","content":"Pretty much the mixed case. The Usurpation, as presented, was done with more of an eye towards removing the Solars and Lunars before they actively became the largest threat to Creation rather than the DBs and Sids deciding they wanted to rule the world and get all the stuff the Solars and Lunars had. The current situation is generally them attempting to make the world the best place it can be while functioning as its protectors, and rulers while enjoying the perks that come from being the god kings and queens of the world. This also means destroying potential threats to the world like newly reborn Solars, Lunars, pretty much anything deemed anathema, and the supporters of anathema.<br /> <br /> In that regard they are good guys. But that doesn't mean they're <b> the </b> good guys. Afterall any big system is going to have problems with it that aren't noticed and there me be flaws that aren't noticed by the higher ups because they don't have to deal with it. Solars and Lunars are a huge threat to world, they're also a great help in defending it and making it work properly. They don't get a choice in exalting, so as far as any of them are concerned the Realm wants them dead for the crime of being chosen to be a hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T19:17:18-07:00","id":1245020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1244970#post1244970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wellll\u2026.<br /> <br /> [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT]<br /> <br /> Certainly, avoid the narrative where the latter means that the former is straightforwardly justified, but it is a bit more nuanced.<br /> <br /> Now more than ever, I think, with things like House Ledaal and how much they're concerned by those Deathlords.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's true and all but I think this forum can agree that exploitative colonialism is bad which firmly places the Scarlet Dynasty in the &quot;bad&quot; camp out-of-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T19:28:01-07:00","id":1245023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245020#post1245020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that's true and all but I think this forum can agree that exploitative colonialism is bad which firmly places the Scarlet Dynasty in the &quot;bad&quot; camp out-of-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those in the Realm who care about that sort of thing prefer the term &quot;necessary evil.&quot; Without a strong hand on the tiller, DB families tend to fragment and war against each other. Similarly, the threshold was a thousand warring states before the armies of the Realm put a stop to it. The Realm's armies oppose rogue gods, Fae marauders, armies of hungry dead, and worse. <i>Someone</i> has to pay for all that and, hey, we DID just save your very souls from being eaten by some monster from the Wyld, so....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T19:53:52-07:00","id":1245033,"title":"","content":"Yes. It's very easy to tsk-tsk about such empires now, but consider how our own ancient history is filled with such empires, and that's <i>without</i> a literally superhuman noble class running it; Representative democracy is a bit of an uphill task to implement in Creation.<br /> <br /> There was a post by... I think someone who is now a writer, but I misremember who, that went to each splat and said &quot;Clearly, X are the heroes. *List amazing accomplishments*. This is why X are the heroes of Exalted.&quot; The point here being that <i>even the Scarlet Realm</i>, which is the closest to a 'villain', is not some cartoonish realm of evil. It was born of a singular remarkable officer and her team on a daring and heroic last-minute scramble through a forbidden ruin to a device that saved the world, and the Dynasty has held the world together since. If you have to be a regular human being in Creation, the Blessed Isle isn't a bad place to be one in, on the whole.<br /> <br /> This is not incompatible with them being a cruel master and colossus with their boot on the throats of millions. If Rome didn't rise to power, some other nation would have and we'd be talking about the horrible practices of Carthage or something now, but they <i>did</i> rise to power and they <i>did</i> do horrible things. That the Realm might provide necessarily stability while simultaneously being kind of shitty might make some heads explode that are used to simple heroes and villains, but both the real world and Creation are more complex.<br /> <br /> After all, it's not like Big Red overthrew an enlightened government to raise her despotism; while the First Age is deliberately unpainted now it was certainly one where the 300 people who shined gold had much more sway than your average human being. This was unlikely to be a representative democracy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T20:03:56-07:00","id":1245034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245033#post1245033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After all, it's not like Big Red overthrew an enlightened government to raise her despotism; while the First Age is deliberately unpainted now it was certainly one where the 300 people who shined gold had much more sway than your average human being. This was unlikely to be a representative democracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor Correction: Her Reddness overthrew/ended the warring states period of Dragonblooded like the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> More to the point, yeah. A point of debate, no doubt, is could the realm be replaced by a better, less boot-on-neck regime. Certainly, the DBs can be as heroic (hell, outcastes? They exist! And not all are on top of massive slave built empires!) and Celestials can be vilianous (I love me some age of Nightmares.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T20:12:30-07:00","id":1245037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Certainly, avoid the narrative where the latter means that the former is straightforwardly justified, but it is a bit more nuanced.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Now more than ever, I think, with things like House Ledaal and how much they're concerned by those Deathlords.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> GCG's quote was made back when fae still had massive numbers, so that's one concern down. As for the anarchy of the threshold... maybe it wouldn't have been in that state if the Realm wasn't constantly sucking wealth out of it, bending its policies to their whims, and supporting whatever strongwoman or strongman went along with them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> With regard to House Ledaal, Thorns was their satrapy. They bled it pallid making war on the Scavenger Lands. Their policy made it easy pickings for the Mask of Winters. They helped dig the hole. Their recent concerns about that one Deathlord above politics are admirable, but they have a long way to go before they count as deeply sympathetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245033#post1245033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. It's very easy to tsk-tsk about such empires now, but consider how our own ancient history is filled with such empires, and that's <i>without</i> a literally superhuman noble class running it; Representative democracy is a bit of an uphill task to implement in Creation.<br /> <br /> There was a post by... I think someone who is now a writer, but I misremember who, that went to each splat and said &quot;Clearly, X are the heroes. *List amazing accomplishments*. This is why X are the heroes of Exalted.&quot; The point here being that <i>even the Scarlet Realm</i>, which is the closest to a 'villain', is not some cartoonish realm of evil. It was born of a singular remarkable officer and her team on a daring and heroic last-minute scramble through a forbidden ruin to a device that saved the world, and the Dynasty has held the world together since. If you have to be a regular human being in Creation, the Blessed Isle isn't a bad place to be one in, on the whole.<br /> <br /> This is not incompatible with them being a cruel master and colossus with their boot on the throats of millions. <b>If Rome didn't rise to power, some other nation would have</b> and we'd be talking about the horrible practices of Carthage or something now, but they <i>did</i> rise to power and they <i>did</i> do horrible things. That the Realm might provide necessarily stability while simultaneously being kind of shitty might make some heads explode that are used to simple heroes and villains, but both the real world and Creation are more complex.<br /> <br /> After all, it's not like Big Red overthrew an enlightened government to raise her despotism; while the First Age is deliberately unpainted now it was certainly one where the 300 people who shined gold had much more sway than your average human being. This was unlikely to be a representative democracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt the certainty of the text that I have placed in bold. We do not inevitably and uncontrollably get worse and worse terrible shit as a natural law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T20:37:23-07:00","id":1245042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1244960#post1244960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereals often make the hard choice of triage and acceptable losses; Romeo and Juliet committing suicide is an acceptable cost to end the unending turmoil between Montague and Capulet.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMHO this is the wrong take on the Flaw of Sidereals. Their problem isn't that have to be cold hearted and make hard choices, it's that <i>they refuse to accept the they could ever be wrong</i>. Their curse is hubris- it <i>doesn't matter</i> what The Realm wants, or what DBs want, or what the Lunars want, all of those people are just <b>Wrong</b> and Sidereals are <b>Right</b> because <b>Destiny Says So</b> and they have a the terrible responsibility of saving us poor fools from our own shortsighted machinations. <b>This is how Sidereals see themselves</b>, the final arbiter on what is the Right Thing To Do.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Its for their own good&quot;<br /> &quot;In 100 years, they'll thank me for this&quot;<br /> &quot;The civilian death toll is with tolerable levels&quot;</i><br /> &quot;<i>It had to be done&quot;</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T20:48:03-07:00","id":1245045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245042#post1245042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IMHO this is the wrong take on the Flaw of Sidereals. Their problem isn't that have to be cold hearted and make hard choices, it's that <i>they refuse to accept the they could ever be wrong</i>. Their curse is hubris- it <i>doesn't matter</i> what The Realm wants, or what DBs want, or what the Lunars want, all of those people are just <b>Wrong</b> and Sidereals are <b>Right</b> because <b>Destiny Says So</b> and they have a the terrible responsibility of saving us poor fools from our own shortsighted machinations. <b>This is how Sidereals see themselves</b>, the final arbiter on what is the Right Thing To Do.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Its for their own good&quot;<br /> &quot;In 100 years, they'll thank me for this&quot;<br /> &quot;The civilian death toll is with tolerable levels&quot;</i><br /> &quot;<i>It had to be done&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Destiny doesn't say so. People tend to miss or ignore the fact that the fact that while they work for the bureau of destiny, it doesn't mean they obey it. They understand fate and thus decide it's course. They didn't shape the realm because destiny said to. They did it because they knew they could CONTROL destiny the best that way. Their curse of hubris has everything to do with what they believe is right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T01:58:49-07:00","id":1245072,"title":"","content":"Many people in the setting will argue whether the Usurpation was wrong, or the Great Uprising was right, and whether that means the Solars or Dragonblood of today are the heroes or villains.<br /> <br /> But they're all wrong. Because a war that happened 1500 years doesn't tell you who is good or bad today. I don't consider your average Dane a bad guy because 1300 years ago the Danish ravaged my country's farms and monasteries. You couldn't tell who were the good guys and bad guys in the Balkan wars of the 90s based on the activities of the Ustashe in the 40s.<br /> I went to a museum in Harbin, China, about the atrocities carried out by Japanese scientists, like live vivisections and infecting people with anthrax. But, while China today likes to invoke these things in their disputes with Japan, I can't say that Japanese atrocities in the 30s and 40s means that China is right and Japan is wrong in today's disputes.<br /> <br /> The only people you could really judge on the Usurpation are the Sidereal and Lunar elders who actually lived through it, like Kejak, Leviathan, Raksi, etc.<br /> <br /> Now, the Scarlet Dynasty is one of the setting's villains. But it's one of the more morally ambiguous ones. They do a lot of evil stuff, but they also do some good stuff. And in a giant Empire, not everyone is exactly the same amount of bad. There are people who want to reform the Dynasty, there are monks who try to battle its excesses, etc. And there are also decadent and corrupt slavers, murderous fanatics, etc. And a lot of just regular people who are trying to get on with their lives and don't really think about the systemic inequalities their society is built on.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the Realm is based on the Chinese Empire, the Roman Empire, and the British Empire. And these giant states are ambiguous. My opinion of them is quite negative, but they have plenty of defenders, and they did do some good stuff. I can't deny the Romans taught the Britons how to write, even if they did enslave and brutalise the Britons and wipe out their history and culture.<br /> I remember when I went to Kenya, people in Nairobi thought the British Empire was awful, whereas people in Mombasa had a much more positive attitude.<br /> I knew a guy from a tribe in the mountains of Myanmar, who told me how great Britain was because a British missionary taught his people writing, medicine, Christianity, and that chopping people's heads off to decorate your village is not cool. But I'm sure people in lowland Myanmar have a very different attitude.<br /> I had a Zambian friend who believed that God allowed the British to conquer Zambia in order to bring them Christianity, which he saw as worth the colonialism. Not that he wanted to be ruled by Britain again, but he didn't see the Empire as entirely a bad thing. I did wonder if his grandparents had the same attitude though.<br /> <br /> Abyssals, Infernals and Raksha are a much more straight-forward evil than the Dynasty. While there may be individual anti-heroes (we have a Raksha in our party, she doesn't really get morality, but she likes hanging around with the PCs and having adventures, and we had a rogue Infernal before), overall they're very definitely the bad guys.<br /> Whereas the Scarlet Dynasty are much more complex. You can't really reform the Neverborn, but reforming the Realm might be possible. An Abyssal may not care if an army of savage barbarians kill everyone in your city, but you may be able to convince a nearby group of Dynasts to save people. House Ledaal is willing to put its efforts towards battling the Abyssals. And while being ruled by the Realm means heavy taxes, it's better than being genocided by Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Overall, the point is that the Dynasty is bad, but not as bad as the setting's other main foes.<br /> <br /> Now... are the Solars good? Several people have mentioned that Solars are more likely than Dynasts to come from oppressed and marginalised people. So they're more likely to be fighting for a better world. But power corrupts, and Solars have a lot of power. So I might say, overall, Solars are probably better than Dragonblood, but it's very much an inidividual thing.<br /> <br /> And this is what it often comes to. I might say, for example, that in WW2 the Brits, French, Russians, Americans, Chinese, etc, were the good guys, and the Germans, Italians, Japanese, Croats, etc, were the bad guys. But that's an overall picture. There were French fascist collaborators. There were Italians who fought Fascism. There were Germans who resisted Nazism. There were plenty of people who went along with their country, but if they were in a different country would have gone along with them as well. Stalin fought the Nazis (eventually) but was definitely a bad guy.<br /> Good and evil are often quite individual. And so I don't think you can say &quot;The Dragonblood&quot; or &quot;The Solars&quot; (or &quot;The Sidereals&quot; or &quot;The Lunars&quot;) are the good or bad guys. Pelleps Delled is a bad guy, but I'm sure lots of people in the North think Yurgen Kaneko is way worse. (Not to mention judging whether people are good or bad is simplistic anyway).<br /> Even within one party of PCs, some of the characters are better or worse than others.<br /> <br /> In the game I play, for example, I'd say:<br /> Loyal Fox, Eclipse - Good, if bitchy<br /> Reborn in Shining Light, Zenith - Good, if foolish and sometimes unwilling to restrain his friends<br /> Golden Hero, Night - He's a liar and an assassin. Anti-hero at best.<br /> Queen Enhenduanna, Eclipse - Gives people prosperity+cool magic powers. Uses magic mind-control to enforce loyalty on nobles and officers.<br /> Fulgens, Dawn - Evil. Definitely evil. Inching towards Hitler-esque levels of evil.<br /> <br /> Really, you can't just judge them as Solars, you have to judge them as individuals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Two last points:<br /> There are loads of Dragonblood in the world who have little to do with the Realm. You can hardly blame Lookshyans who defend the River Province from the Realm, for the Realm.<br /> No-one knows about the Great Curse (except maybe Jupiter and Lytek, and they're not telling). Which is something that's probably quite important in judging the morality of Solars past and present (if a Solar turns a thousand beautiful people into statues to decorate their manor, is that the Solar's fault, or the Neverborn who cursed her with madness?), but no one can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-12-2018, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T02:02:08-07:00","id":1245074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245037#post1245037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt the certainty of the text that I have placed in bold. We do not inevitably and uncontrollably get worse and worse terrible shit as a natural law.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... That's literally what happened. There were other city-states that competed with early Rome. When Rome dominated the Italian peninsula, there were other regional powers.<br /> <br /> And a military empire tends to develop, historically, because its the most straightforward arrangement: bigger army diplomacy. But it also has the most fraught moments of power transfer. Lots of empires never outlived the first emperor and their heir.<br /> <br /> The Realm is a pretty solid example of that, at year zero. It only lasted as long as it did because it was run by a long-lived superhuman. Without her Scarletness around to force compliance, starting with armies and ending with rendering your lands uninhabitable with a magical superweapon, it's all falling apart rapidly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T03:51:03-07:00","id":1245079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245020#post1245020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that's true and all but I think this forum can agree that exploitative colonialism is bad which firmly places the Scarlet Dynasty in the &quot;bad&quot; camp out-of-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do I put this...<br /> <br /> I agree with that, and have in the past used points about the harmful legacy of colonialism in the modern day to argue against some people taking the idea that the actions of the Realm are inevitable or preferable at face value. That is to say, the Realm hypes itself, and I would argue for people to apply critical thinking that keeps them from buying into that hype.<br /> <br /> I don't apply those standards to the <i>characters</i>; for there to be fictional characters within the setting, from multiple angles, who buy into the Realm's hype (even if their attitude on the Realm itself is to take over in that role for it) is not only to be expected, but something that I'm not inclined to write them off for and pass judgement on. That's partially my perspective on pre-modern history, and it's particularly how I approach a lot of fiction, because fiction affords me that level of detachment. It provides an environment in which to explore certain ideas and scenarios and perspectives without real world consequences, so long as I give consideration for how such is influencing me.<br /> <br /> So while I would find the principle of the Realm's imperialism to be bad with little to no ambiguity, I think there's a reasonable place to approach and discuss it from its own side of things, that has more complexity than just indulging in playing the bad guys or being one of the lone good cops in a corrupt system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245037#post1245037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GCG's quote was made back when fae still had massive numbers, so that's one concern down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that we can only speculate on how far back the idea of having the Raksha as broken remnants goes, but even with that point there are still a few considerations.<br /> <br /> One being the possibility that, even if they aren't limitless hordes, the Fair Folk still have the kinds of numbers to make a lot of trouble if they were sufficiently motivated and didn't fear the Realm Defence Grid. How many would it take to cause devastation on a grand scale? Much more than the Mongols had? Not to mention the more esoteric kinds of threats like what the new one in Adversaries is about; things that require fewer bodies.<br /> <br /> The other consideration is whether or not people in Creation are supposed to be aware of the current state of the Raksha, or are still running off of the image of them from the last time that they almost destroyed the world. That includes the Realm; the personalities behind that imperialism would need to account for people who really do believe that there's another threat waiting just past the edge of the door.<br /> <br /> On both counts, I'll note that Second Edition maintained the element of the Scavenger Lands backstory in which a large Fair Folk invasion came close to utterly devastating that region right up into Masters of Jade.<br /> <br /> Finally, there's the matter of how the updated version can probably reassign a lot of the threat of Fair Folk to Lunars. Disregarding the subject of who started it, there are still people in desperate fear for their lives in the face of the Lunars, many of whom probably didn't really do anything to deserve it (by which I mean random peasants and citizens in the face of some Lunars that are perhaps not going to be very discriminating).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the anarchy of the threshold... maybe it wouldn't have been in that state if the Realm wasn't constantly sucking wealth out of it, bending its policies to their whims, and supporting whatever strongwoman or strongman went along with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the backstory that the Realm had in the prior two Editions, I think there's a not unreasonable basis for the nascent Realm's rulers to have formed a basis for what things would be like without them in the form of the Seven Tigers, the centuries of fighting over Chiaroscuro, or Bagrash Kol. It's not altogether rational, but it's a level of irrationality that I can't particularly blame anybody for, if I assume that the fictional characters are working from the tendency for simplistic world views that large numbers of actual people do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regard to House Ledaal, Thorns was their satrapy. They bled it pallid making war on the Scavenger Lands. Their policy made it easy pickings for the Mask of Winters. They helped dig the hole. Their recent concerns about that one Deathlord above politics are admirable, but they have a long way to go before they count as deeply sympathetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all a very good point about the complexity of the situation that prevents it from being a simplistic binary of good and bad; I would personally throw in the point that Ledaal is presented as considering making unprovoked war on Nellens for the sake of securing a number of resources and other considerations for the sake of pursuing their agenda against the Deathlords. It's still an overall more complicated situation than them being the bad guys.<br /> <br /> As for sympathy, different people have different standards. My own baseline is something like &quot;is capable of crying&quot;.<br /> <br /> As an answer to the original question, I would say that there are many Dragon Blooded that are good guys to somebody, and many of them would be bad guys along similar lines to, say, Loki from the Marvel Cinematic Universe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T06:03:08-07:00","id":1245095,"title":"","content":"The Realm and Dragon-Blooded are good <i>enough</i> that you can play a straightforward loyal Realm patriot Dynast and be playing a good guy.<br /> <br /> The Realm and Dragon-Blooded are evil <i>enough</i> that you can play a straightforward rebel leader and be playing a good guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T07:09:17-07:00","id":1245104,"title":"","content":"It's part of the appeal of Exalted to some that, 17 years after publishing the first book, no one still can really say as to the answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Though, the usual stance by the guys who write the game has probably most often been been that the Solars are probably the better horse to back; at least in the longer term, as the other powers are somewhat inept to ultimately defend Creation, dependent on magical artefacts and the like that get lost and which they can't really recreate. (Which I say as someone who has for most of the time since Exalted came out, preferred to invert this stance to the maximum, in favour of the lowest of the Chosen taking control of their own destiny, and refusing to serve as mere soldiers of the &quot;superiors&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T12:59:38-07:00","id":1245168,"title":"","content":"Wow that's a lot of good responses. The players and the characters in my game are both new to exalted so their in game and out of game knowledge. Their Charactera definitely fall on the good side as solars. However as I watch them wreak havok on every nation or tribe they encounter for good purposes I can't help but imagine what happena when they limit break. A lot of people will suffer and it's scary to think of creation in their hands if only for that reason.<br /> <br /> Right now the players have just arrived in mahalanka and they are making choices between siding with a clearly evil raksi to attack the realm or fleeing raksi and searching out a more clearly good way. Either way their decision will effect thousands. <br /> <br /> They are just discovering knowledge of the great curse and the prophecy and they think it's all bs just meant to keep the dragon blooded in charge. Seeing how much they effect entire nation's I wonder who signed right.<br /> <br /> Based on these comments I think my plan is probably to have both good and very evil dragon blooded as opponents. The characters can decide for themselves the value of the realm but dragon blooded individuals will run the gamut of morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T13:33:48-07:00","id":1245175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245168#post1245168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However as I watch them wreak havok on every nation or tribe they encounter for good purposes I can't help but imagine what happena when they limit break. A lot of people will suffer and it's scary to think of creation in their hands if only for that reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, that reminds me of a lot of Exalted games I've played. PCs just cause chaos and destruction whether they're good or evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T13:42:55-07:00","id":1245177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245168#post1245168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on these comments I think my plan is probably to have both good and very evil dragon blooded as opponents. The characters can decide for themselves the value of the realm but dragon blooded individuals will run the gamut of morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have some good Dragon Blooded. Maybe have a scene where a group of Dragon Blooded are protecting a village from being overrun by horrible monsters (maybe Raksi's beastmen who are coming for their share of human flesh). It's also not hard to show off some oppressive ones too. <br /> <br /> Ultimately Creation is a complicated world, and just as it's impossible to point to any group of people in real life and label them as universally good, it's likewise impossible to do that to any group in Creation. But, even among the Realm there are absolutely heroes and champions who are going to do their best to help people out. By no means are all of them completely selfish assholes who get off on hurting people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T13:52:37-07:00","id":1245178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245074#post1245074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But... That's literally what happened. There were other city-states that competed with early Rome. When Rome dominated the Italian peninsula, there were other regional powers.<br /> <br /> And a military empire tends to develop, historically, because its the most straightforward arrangement: bigger army diplomacy. But it also has the most fraught moments of power transfer. Lots of empires never outlived the first emperor and their heir.<br /> <br /> The Realm is a pretty solid example of that, at year zero. It only lasted as long as it did because it was run by a long-lived superhuman. Without her Scarletness around to force compliance, starting with armies and ending with rendering your lands uninhabitable with a magical superweapon, it's all falling apart rapidly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The Scarlet Empress is supposed to be kind of an expy of China's First Emperor, in that both of them apparently decided that they needed to be unquestionably in charge and ensure that they made any and all important decisions. And, when they considered the possibility of a succession crisis, rather than engaging in governmental reform, they both decided to just live forever instead. Granted, the Scarlet Empress did a much better job of it than Qin Shi Huang, but they both ran up against the same problem: They built empires that were designed to fall apart without them and then they went away.<br /> <br /> See also: <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/QinShihuangdi\" target=\"_blank\">http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Sp.../QinShihuangdi</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey C. Grabowski</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> g_c_grabowski - 03/25/2004 01:08:34 - <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#8ffdeee6e1ebe0e8cff8e7e6fbeaa2f8e0e3e9a1ece0e2\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"c7b5a6aea9a3a8a087b0afaeb3a2eab0a8aba1e9a4a8aa\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><br /> I laughed my ass off at Wookie's post. =) <i> Context: A humorous rewriting of the essential dialogue of the movie, displaying plainly apparent praise for China, Communism, Fearless Leaders, etc </i><br /> Here's my thoughts, in response to Jason;<br /> I think the Partition is just one bit of the issue. The Chinese state had every appurtenance of organized modernity -- an organized bureaucracy, complex financial instruments, formal education. Yet they also had a totally centralized executive with no functional mechanism of non-hereditary succession. This cursed the state to endless cycles of dynastic warfare and left the entire nation open to manipulation by whoever could get their hand up the butt of the Man Standing Alone, which historically was something of a national sport.<br /> Obviously it's not the only issue -- the anti-military and inward/backward-looking sentiments of Confucianism didn't help. However.... I don't have a problem seeing the endless cycle of the emperor's advisors overpowering him and ruining the state for their own profit until there's an unmet crisis of empire that the decayed imperial structure can't meet as a direct legacy of the First Emperor. He consolidated power in China and ended the Age of War by creating a state with a single point of failure and an ethic that favored the state (in the person of the emperor) over the individual, and thus made it nearly impossible to protect the /office/ of the emperor because so much of the office was concentrated in the Son of Heaven, and no safer than that one person.<br /> The Chinese did lots of brilliant things. It's an awesome culture, and I have a whole shelf full of books about it. I just think that the concentration of the state authority on the semi-divine personage of the emperor and the consequent demeaning of the individual can be laid largely at his feet. He could just as easily have used the abdication of the Sage Kings to justify some sort of functional succession mechanism. The great thing about democracy it that distributes the mechanism of succession in such a fashion that it's difficult to hijack.<br /> It's obvious the Emperor confronted this issue, he just chose to provide for it by eating mercury rather than establishing something that could genuinely sustain the nation, and I do think the consequences were long-ranging. You can say it?s not his fault by framing the situation as one where the long-term negative consequences are external and unknowable but they aren?t, or if they were, then it's really his fault for doing things without knowing what the true consequences are.<br /> I mean, it's not like he was the world's greatest primitive agronomist, working all along in good faith, never knowing that the perfect tomato would serve as the catalyst for an age of war by enabling massive armies and extended campaigns. The guy made himself sole, uncontested, brutal, totalitarian ruler of his vast and populous nation. Inasmuch as there was a place for the buck to stop, he moved that place to his throne room. I don?t really feel bad blaming him for anything that sprang from that because he methodically made himself the only person /to/ blame.<br /> G.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Shi_Huang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/QinShiHuang19century.jpg/960px-QinShiHuang19century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Shi_Huang\" target=\"_blank\"> Qin Shi Huang - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Shi_Huang\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Shi_Huang </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I think that it is possible that the Scarlet Empress could have tried to create something that would work without her. One could argue that she didn't because she wanted to have the Sword of Creation ready for the next giant attack on Creation but feared what it might do in the hands of anyone else. One could also argue that she didn't want to be murdered or give up her enormously high standard of living. Ultimately, for whatever reason, she did not, and now everyone is paying for her failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:28:44-07:00","id":1245203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245079#post1245079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose that we can only speculate on how far back the idea of having the Raksha as broken remnants goes, but even with that point there are still a few considerations.<br /> <br /> One being the possibility that, even if they aren't limitless hordes, the Fair Folk still have the kinds of numbers to make a lot of trouble if they were sufficiently motivated and didn't fear the Realm Defence Grid. How many would it take to cause devastation on a grand scale? Much more than the Mongols had? Not to mention the more esoteric kinds of threats like what the new one in Adversaries is about; things that require fewer bodies.<br /> <br /> The other consideration is whether or not people in Creation are supposed to be aware of the current state of the Raksha, or are still running off of the image of them from the last time that they almost destroyed the world. That includes the Realm; the personalities behind that imperialism would need to account for people who really do believe that there's another threat waiting just past the edge of the door.<br /> <br /> On both counts, I'll note that Second Edition maintained the element of the Scavenger Lands backstory in which a large Fair Folk invasion came close to utterly devastating that region right up into Masters of Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to mention something about the Diamond Court, but it seems I was not recalling who threw them down correctly (it was the Tepet Legions rather than Guild-backed local mortals, but then, the Realm has lost most of the descendants of those who managed that feat...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, there's the matter of how the updated version can probably reassign a lot of the threat of Fair Folk to Lunars. Disregarding the subject of who started it, there are still people in desperate fear for their lives in the face of the Lunars, many of whom probably didn't really do anything to deserve it (by which I mean random peasants and citizens in the face of some Lunars that are perhaps not going to be very discriminating). </div> </div> </div>But exactly who started that conflict is rather important, because it did shape Lunars into what they later became.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Going by the backstory that the Realm had in the prior two Editions, I think there's a not unreasonable basis for the nascent Realm's rulers to have formed a basis for what things would be like without them in the form of the Seven Tigers, the centuries of fighting over Chiaroscuro, or Bagrash Kol. </div> </div> </div>The Realm knew nothing about Bagrash Kol until refugees showed up in distant lands. They could have tried to paint a picture of it to go along with their propaganda efforts, but that would have meant coming to grips with a mere mortal sorcerer's holdings that were doing better than the Realm, so they probably don't touch that one very much. Meanwhile, you also have the Scavenger Lands repeatedly repulsing the Realm's advances even though they're a disparate bunch of governments that are often keeping to each other. Part of that is due to squatting on dangerous geomantic relics, part of it is because the Scarlet Empress realized that she could use the apparent threat of the Scavenger Lands to keep her subjects in line, but those two parts wouldn't come together if there weren't some genuine and significant, if grudging, cooperation without conquest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not altogether rational, but it's a level of irrationality that I can't particularly blame anybody for, if I assume that the fictional characters are working from the tendency for simplistic world views that large numbers of actual people do. </div> </div> </div>Well, at this point, it also has a kind of Lord of the Flies effect on the populace of the Blessed Isle. They're raised on the glories of the Realm, taught that everyone else is inferior, and fed lines about how, without a strong authority, everyone would eat each other (mostly not literally), when, in fact, that only applies to them, having been raised to brutally apply boots to throats when ordered or to give the order unhesitatingly, and not to anyone else as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's all a very good point about the complexity of the situation that prevents it from being a simplistic binary of good and bad; I would personally throw in the point that Ledaal is presented as considering making unprovoked war on Nellens for the sake of securing a number of resources and other considerations for the sake of pursuing their agenda against the Deathlords. It's still an overall more complicated situation than them being the bad guys.<br /> <br /> As for sympathy, different people have different standards. My own baseline is something like &quot;is capable of crying&quot;. </div> </div> </div>A large quantity of Dynasts would probably view that as a sign of weakness and avoid it wherever possible, even to the point of denying their feelings on a matter.<br /> <br /> (Also I think I started drifting into method writing for a Lunar character's background fiction there, sorry.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an answer to the original question, I would say that there are many Dragon Blooded that are good guys to somebody, and many of them would be bad guys along similar lines to, say, Loki from the Marvel Cinematic Universe. </div> </div> </div>Even so, going back to the OP, we're expected to see more good than harm in Solars coming back. It's the intent of the text starting with Solars and not Dragon-Blooded, or at least a significant portion of it. That means more Daces and Fire Orchids and fewer of the Anathematic Five from the Caste books (Lyta, Wind, Fehim, Havesh, and the Mirror Flag, even though at least Wind isn't really bad by most readers' definition, and few people know what to make of the Mirror Flag, but she does seem committed to punching upward, at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:33:37-07:00","id":1245208,"title":"","content":"The number one thing to remember, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3901\" data-vbnamecard=\"3901\">RadioFreeDeath</a> , is that extremely few people are ever evil 'for the lulz' unless they're morons (see: 2e Infernals from the Lost Chapters). A good 'evil' character should have reasons for their evil, even if they're terrible ones.<br /> <br /> A Lunar and her warband ravage the lands and burn the farms of villagers because she is denying ground to the Dragon-Blooded, undermining their regime and destabilizing them piece by piece, not because she's an an atavistic anarchist who thinks civilization bad and wipes her rear with poison ivy instead of toilet paper so she doesn't 'become soft' (unless you want her to be a moron that can be corrected and educated, but eh, that's not a great arc).<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blooded extracts harsh tribute because his family expects it from the lands he governs in order to fund the house's place in the civil war looming on the horizon, typically not because he likes seeing starving peasants or something. He may gain personal rewards from it as well, luxury earned with the blood, sweat, and tears of those beneath him, but it is that luxury and obligation that is why he will make an example of a peasant, not because he can't get excited enough to play with his concubines without first whipping an innocent person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:47:33-07:00","id":1245216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245178#post1245178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no. The Scarlet Empress is supposed to be kind of an expy of China's First Emperor, in that both of them apparently decided that they needed to be unquestionably in charge and ensure that they made any and all important decisions. And, when they considered the possibility of a succession crisis, rather than engaging in governmental reform, they both decided to just live forever instead. Granted, the Scarlet Empress did a much better job of it than Qin Shi Huang, but they both ran up against the same problem: They built empires that were designed to fall apart without them and then they went away.<br /> <br /> See also: <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/QinShihuangdi\" target=\"_blank\">http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Sp.../QinShihuangdi</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, talk about GCG quotes that are a blast from the past; I think the parallelism falls down to some degree - the Empress didn't just create a system that couldn't function without her, she created a system with deep, engineered, internal conflict between any would be successors.<br /> <br /> (Though on a more general note, and really a bit of a tangent, I think his ideas of QSH setting a powerful precedent for China are to some degree open to question. Further some of the ideas of China as unusually lacking in respect for &quot;the individual&quot; and as atypically centralized may have not aged well. <br /> <br /> I believe historical ideas about Chinese government I usually encounter today tend towards China not being unusually absolutist across its history. Early modern states, largely in Europe, which (unusually) had some degree of representative institutions have tended to forge them for the purposes of acquiring taxes, in order to fund a more regimented, state controlled society with proportionately larger military than in China of the time. Representative institutions were not born out of some sort of wise choices by the philosophers.<br /> <br /> The story I usually encounter is that China largely opted out of this path, for a lower taxed, less regulating and less interfering centralized state that did not require &quot;compromise&quot; to the authority of the Confucian elite via representative politics, albeit even the merit based promotion of that elite itself offered some form of representation within government for the Chinese class of gentry. China avoided representation in government by having a relatively smaller, more minimal state. And the Confucian bureaucracy moralized this as the correct path, by forming an official ideology that money should be in society with producers (that, is they favoured money being with &quot;the individual&quot; rather than taxed by &quot;the state&quot;). China could do this with some degree of stability because it was so vast, and the military mainly focused on the northern steppes, but in time this low tax, low military expenditure, weakly centralized state had problems...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T18:34:14-07:00","id":1245270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245178#post1245178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it is possible that the Scarlet Empress could have tried to create something that would work without her. One could argue that she didn't because she wanted to have the Sword of Creation ready for the next giant attack on Creation but feared what it might do in the hands of anyone else. One could also argue that she didn't want to be murdered or give up her enormously high standard of living. Ultimately, for whatever reason, she did not, and now everyone is paying for her failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my own games Realm's dysfunction and lack of a succession system was very much intentional on the part of the Empress. I mean, she didn't plan on dying any time soon and imagine if she had gone, &quot;Hey Mnemon, you're my heir, but since I plan to live forever, unless foul play occurs and <i>someone</i> murders me, you'll probably be dead long before I ever am.&quot; That probably wouldn't be a great idea. <br /> <br /> Further, she just plain didn't trust Chejop any further than she could throw the Sword of Creation, and quite a bit of her paranoia (well deserved considering there were at least 300 shapeshifting Exalted who wanted her dead) was directed at him. The two were allies of convenience and nothing more. Their goals happened to be in alignment for the moment - she wanted to stay alive and remain in power. He wanted to ensure Creation's stability and the best way to do that was to work with the Scarlet Empress, but that could easily change in the future. So she wouldn't want to make it too tempting or easy for Chejop to decide that it would be best for Creation if the Scarlet Empress were replaced with a more pliable successor.<br /> <br /> Knowing that the Realm would collapse into civil war if she vanished simply made it less likely that Chejop would decide to try and get rid of her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T21:59:43-07:00","id":1245332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245270#post1245270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my own games Realm's dysfunction and lack of a succession system was very much intentional on the part of the Empress. I mean, she didn't plan on dying any time soon and imagine if she had gone, &amp;quot;Hey Mnemon, you're my heir, but since I plan to live forever, unless foul play occurs and <i>someone</i> murders me, you'll probably be dead long before I ever am.&amp;quot; That probably wouldn't be a great idea. <br /> <br /> Further, she just plain didn't trust Chejop any further than she could throw the Sword of Creation, and quite a bit of her paranoia (well deserved considering there were at least 300 shapeshifting Exalted who wanted her dead) was directed at him. The two were allies of convenience and nothing more. Their goals happened to be in alignment for the moment - she wanted to stay alive and remain in power. He wanted to ensure Creation's stability and the best way to do that was to work with the Scarlet Empress, but that could easily change in the future. So she wouldn't want to make it too tempting or easy for Chejop to decide that it would be best for Creation if the Scarlet Empress were replaced with a more pliable successor.<br /> <br /> Knowing that the Realm would collapse into civil war if she vanished simply made it less likely that Chejop would decide to try and get rid of her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that\u2019s my take on it too. I just wanted to acknowledge that there are a couple of points that could be argued to be somewhat noble about what she did, but there\u2019s really no way to defend how she built this empire to be incapable of functioning without her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T00:07:29-07:00","id":1245349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245168#post1245168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on these comments I think my plan is probably to have both good and very evil dragon blooded as opponents. The characters can decide for themselves the value of the realm but dragon blooded individuals will run the gamut of morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have a mind to complicating which is which; one can be a genuine and accomplished hero of the people, saaaaay a Peleps who goes around investigating crimes, passing judgements generally considered to be fair, and fighting evil priests, but as a person they're extremely haughty, status conscious and uncompromisingly harsh, while elsewhere you have somebody charming, personable, beloved by friends and the unusual Dynast that is more active and loving in the lives of their children, whose work consists of something that fairly directly contributes to the oppression of the people of a satrapy (say something like... a freelance consultant for satraps who advises on policies for the satrap to promote in the local ruler that will maximize tributary profits while minimizing local resistance, and ways of dealing with objections by the common people that are harsh and direct).<br /> <br /> I've got my eye on a couple of other posts here, but I'll need to fully wake up first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T00:39:40-07:00","id":1245351,"title":"","content":"The other take is that this is how she intended to choose a successor. If she ever died she didn't want someone unsuitable just slipping into her place, no, they'd need to <i>earn</i> it.<br /> <br /> Have the whole thing collapse, and then whoever comes out on top in the ensuing power struggle will definitely have the chops to lead the Dragon Blooded in her place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T01:10:43-07:00","id":1245357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245270#post1245270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my own games Realm's dysfunction and lack of a succession system was very much intentional on the part of the Empress. I mean, she didn't plan on dying any time soon and imagine if she had gone, &quot;Hey Mnemon, you're my heir, but since I plan to live forever, unless foul play occurs and <i>someone</i> murders me, you'll probably be dead long before I ever am.&quot; That probably wouldn't be a great idea.<br /> <br /> Further, she just plain didn't trust Chejop any further than she could throw the Sword of Creation, and quite a bit of her paranoia (well deserved considering there were at least 300 shapeshifting Exalted who wanted her dead) was directed at him. The two were allies of convenience and nothing more. Their goals happened to be in alignment for the moment - she wanted to stay alive and remain in power. He wanted to ensure Creation's stability and the best way to do that was to work with the Scarlet Empress, but that could easily change in the future. So she wouldn't want to make it too tempting or easy for Chejop to decide that it would be best for Creation if the Scarlet Empress were replaced with a more pliable successor.<br /> <br /> Knowing that the Realm would collapse into civil war if she vanished simply made it less likely that Chejop would decide to try and get rid of her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, by the way that it was written in the original book, the Thousand Hazy Paths was started as a somewhat extreme response to a random assassination attempt that came distressingly close to succeeding.<br /> <br /> Whatever one opted to make of the Empress in precise details, I found the general inclination of the backstory to be one in which she did have a genuine concern for the fate of the world, at least at the beginning, and was terrified at the possibility of what would happen if they immediately resumed the old kind of fighting. She would almost certainly prefer not to die, but I could see her at least having an attitude towards Chejop in which there's enough respect to presume he would install somebody competent (or perhaps rather, she would respect him in a manner as to assume that she shares her perspective that nobody else is competent). I think that she was far more worried about being killed by some random opportunist, who wouldn't know what they were in for.<br /> <br /> Hell, she may have even opted to develop a system of succession were it not for the fact that one of her earliest children was Ragara. Across all Editions, he's just been... the worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T01:34:00-07:00","id":1245359,"title":"","content":"Are the Dragonblooded good? Some of them are, yes, Is The Realm good? Thaaat's thornier.<br /> <br /> It's important to realize that most, if not all of Exalted's major powers are, by our standards, pretty bad. It's 100% legal to own your fellow human beings as property in most of Creation, and most people think that's just how the world shakes out. If you took the exploitation, greed and human misery out of Nexus, Gem, Harborhead or Paragon, just to pick four major cities out of a hat, they'd probably collapse into screaming anarchy in a week, and take a large chunk of an entire Direction's economy with them.<br /> <br /> So..Good by whose standard? If I'm using mine, nearly every society in Creation is varying degrees of evil, and The Realm can only be called worse due to scale. You're not going to find a Good nation unless you make one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T01:54:25-07:00","id":1245363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245203#post1245203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But exactly who started that conflict is rather important, because it did shape Lunars into what they later became.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but my point is that a subject like this becomes complicated by the fact that, when portrayed realistically, a genuinely wronged group still has a capacity to respond in a manner that is liable to have a lot of collateral damage (or very deliberate damage towards targets that might be dubious), which can generate a genuine fear in the other side.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of Star Trek: Deep Space Nine and its portrayal of the Bajoran Resistance: the show was very clear on how the occupation of their home world entailed a number of atrocities, but it didn't shy away from the idea that they had no compunctions about attacks that would kill civilians or even occasionally their own people, and we'd thus see Cardassians of various ranks whose stated motivation would be primarily defending their own lives or the lives of their people.<br /> <br /> Which would then get into scenarios of trying to discourage resistance with indiscriminate reprisals, and it all became a vicious cycle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, you also have the Scavenger Lands repeatedly repulsing the Realm's advances even though they're a disparate bunch of governments that are often keeping to each other. Part of that is due to squatting on dangerous geomantic relics, part of it is because the Scarlet Empress realized that she could use the apparent threat of the Scavenger Lands to keep her subjects in line, but those two parts wouldn't come together if there weren't some genuine and significant, if grudging, cooperation without conquest.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, there's a point to be made that no narrative is comprehensive, and that it would make sense for the Realm to have rationalizations away for the River Province. On the other, one could portray the Realm as viewing the Scavenger Lands as being in precisely the kind of anarchy that they want to avoid throughout the Threshold, and not being entirely wrong about that. I can certainly imagine Dynasts who might visit Nexus and come away with their world view validated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A large quantity of Dynasts would probably view that as a sign of weakness and avoid it wherever possible, even to the point of denying their feelings on a matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their hurt is on the inside!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even so, going back to the OP, we're expected to see more good than harm in Solars coming back. It's the intent of the text starting with Solars and not Dragon-Blooded, or at least a significant portion of it. That means more Daces and Fire Orchids and fewer of the Anathematic Five from the Caste books (Lyta, Wind, Fehim, Havesh, and the Mirror Flag, even though at least Wind isn't really bad by most readers' definition, and few people know what to make of the Mirror Flag, but she does seem committed to punching upward, at least).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that I agree in principle, disagree on some of the specifics, and wouldn't want to go into more detail here because it would be getting off topic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T04:53:13-07:00","id":1245403,"title":"","content":"It might be a fun forum game, to suggest a story hook where some Chosen of some splat are made out to be villains, and the response is to concoct a fun, in-story reason why they might be doing what they're doing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T05:18:08-07:00","id":1245405,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, one might take a few worthwhile things in how to portray the Realm with complexity and nuance with the presentation of the Cardassians in Deep Space Nine.<br /> <br /> Gul Dukat in particular, one of the all time great villains; an all around terrible person, but multi-faceted in his being so, quite compelling even at his worst and with a certain charm that can occasionally make you forget the worst (a thing that happens to characters dealing with him every now and then), and with a few... it would be inaccurate to call them redeeming characteristics, but things that he does that are not terrible, and even laudable in their own right. His activities a combination of internalized values that he expresses uncritically from his imperialistic, militaristic and authoritarian society*, and his own unpleasant personality. In particular, many of his rationalizations of his activities are highly self-serving, and it's likely that a lot of his reprisals for repeated attempts on his life were driven by a wounded vanity.<br /> <br /> * One of the compelling and somewhat laudable things that he does is, when his homeland is being invaded by Klingons and he manages to acquire valuable intelligence, he is enraged at how the government is unwilling to use that intelligence to fight back and turns down the opportunity to resume a high-ranking office that he'd been forced out of, opting to instead go on a one-ship guerrilla campaign against the Klingons. But he frames this in terms of his people having become weak and cowardly, and that his willingness to fight means that he's the only real Cardassian left in existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T05:30:45-07:00","id":1245411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245351#post1245351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other take is that this is how she intended to choose a successor. If she ever died she didn't want someone unsuitable just slipping into her place, no, they'd need to <i>earn</i> it.<br /> <br /> Have the whole thing collapse, and then whoever comes out on top in the ensuing power struggle will definitely have the chops to lead the Dragon Blooded in her place.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of behind the motivations for what would IRL be somewhat close to the post-Redness Dynasty, the open competition between large numbers of Ottoman claimants - <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/AskHistorians/comments/1xq85a/why_was_succession_to_the_ottoman_throne_open_and/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/AskHistoria...rone_open_and/</a>. Legitimacy derives from leaders who prove themselves in open warfare, and those that don't are more or less wiped out. <br /> <br /> In that case it seems to boil down to propagation of traditions among Turko-Mongolic groups, to a situation of a more rigid settled empire where they probably were not quite suited. That's not quite something which makes sense for the Realm, which doesn't share that sort of origin at all really, but you can explain it within these motivations for the Scarlet Empress that others have covered. <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245203#post1245203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even so, going back to the OP, we're expected to see more good than harm in Solars coming back. It's the intent of the text starting with Solars and not Dragon-Blooded, or at least a significant portion of it. That means more Daces and Fire Orchids and fewer of the Anathematic Five from the Caste books (Lyta, Wind, Fehim, Havesh, and the Mirror Flag, even though at least Wind isn't really bad by most readers' definition, and few people know what to make of the Mirror Flag, but she does seem committed to punching upward, at least).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that's the intent, on the whole (&quot;more good than harm&quot;), and I would agree the reborn Solars are generally presented as more virtuous than the Dragonblooded (and to an extent the Sidereals and Lunars) who are of more mediocre virtue, and that the Solars are less compromised by worldly politics.<br /> <br /> The questions around them, where there's room for &quot;more harm than good&quot; should you choose to approach that angle, often revolve less around whether they are directly malevolent or purely self interested when Exalted (though such people are among their number), as whether <br /> <br /> a) loose cannons with aspirations to improve society or visions of grandeur will ultimately have a positive effect on the system, or whether events will become larger and are larger than the talents and assumptions can manage, and their revolutions and campaigns will get out of control - the arguments against revolution and against vigilante action<br /> <br /> b) whether their decision making will be twisted by the Great Curse at the worst moments, ruining what they try to accomplish, and whether it will gradually harden and coarsen them to be worse than they are - the idea that the Great Curse will make tragic heroes of them<br /> <br /> c) Solar rule, since they are so individually excellent and irreplaceable, won't tend towards the kind of fragile centralization of authority into a limited number of persons, along the lines of what we've discussed ITT for the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> But generally this is not the main assumption that is the default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T06:46:36-07:00","id":1245447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the return of solars a good thing? Is it the only way to stop a variety of other threats to creation the dragon blooded can't handle? What am I missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>These questions are the central theme of the game. There\u2019s no objectively correct answer. <br /> <br /> The central question of a Solar game is will you succumb to the hubris of your godlike power, or manage to stay grounded in the humane? <br /> <br /> As the ST you can revel in tempting them to flex their power and triggering their Limit Break. It doesn\u2019t take much in my experience \ud83d\ude08<br /> <br /> Bear in mind that the Primordials\u2019 death curse effected *all* of the Exalted. The Usurpation is also a reflection of titanomachy, and fueled just as much by hubris on the part of the Sidereals and Terrestrials. It too is an inversion of \u201cnatural order\u201d in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11690,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","user":"mizzlfoshizzl","date":". 08-13-2018, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T07:05:11-07:00","id":1245455,"title":"","content":"Are the Solars good guys? That depends on how your players are playing them. Thats the whole point. Are they working against a corrupt Realm, freeing slaves, fighting demons and fair folk for a just cause, etc? If they are, then they are taking on an idealistic Solar Exalted role and could be the good guys. HOWEVER, if your game is anything like most of the games I've run, and the players are a bunch of murderhobos and go around collecting loot, punching random gods to see how powerful they are, or just being general, well, PCs, then they are pretty much EXACTLY what the dragon blooded are afraid of, and they're not the good guys. I also think the great curse is a lie, and that the Solars went &quot;insane&quot; because humans get bored after 1000+ years of life, and their vices just get worse and worse over time. That's up to you though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24418-dracheau","name":"Dracheau","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T07:18:12-07:00","id":1245458,"title":"","content":"Well, the great curse isn't a <i>lie</i> because nobody is telling it. Nobody in-setting knows.<br /> <br /> You could, however, decide that the game elements that by RAW are supposed to be the result of a curse cast by dying primordials are, in fact, just what the exalted are like though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T07:44:03-07:00","id":1245471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys#post1244941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The great curse seems like an incredible threat to creation. Sure things havn't been perfect since that time, but having a bunch of insane solars and lunars be better? My players think the great curse is a lie because they are clearly the good guys. I want to present my story from that perspective since my characters are solars, but I am having a hard time making sense of it in my own head. How is the return of solars a good thing? Is it the only way to stop a variety of other threats to creation the dragon blooded can't handle? What am I missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing the fact that the Great Curse didn't just affect Solars and Lunars. It also affected the Sidreal Exalted (and was probably the reason they instigated The Usurption) and the Dragon-Blooded. All Exalted are a threat to Creation when the Great Curse comes into play. If you want to rationalize it, Solars have the most power to do good. However, they conversely have the most power to do harm. So, if they can keep a handle on their curse, they can effect more good than the other types of exalts. That could make them &quot;heroes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T08:02:45-07:00","id":1245477,"title":"","content":"Oh, I missed this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The great curse seems like an incredible threat to creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Of course it is.<br /> <br /> At least thirty percent of the game is about handling incredible threats to Creation.<br /> <br /> Look at the parameters of the thing, and try to find compelling stories about dealing with it.<br /> <br /> I have not, for several years now, understood why so many people came away from the Great Curse with &quot;Solars inevitably turn terrible and will wreck everything&quot; or &quot;my gameplay is impeded by randomly doing something evil and crazy&quot;. I wasn't part of these discussions until late into Second Edition, so did that only become a thing when it became possible to gain Limit from resisting unnatural mental influence?<br /> <br /> Or... I can't recall, did suppressing Virtues ever give Limit? Was it just the one, the one that the Virtue Flaw was connected to? You suppressed Compassion too many times, you'd get the Red Rage coming down on you? That was probably still a thing in First Edition, right?<br /> <br /> Seriously, it's weird that people so often seem to detach the circumstances of the Great Curse from literally everything that can trigger it.<br /> <br /> My point is, one good way to make a compelling story about struggling in opposition to the Great Curse is to maybe tailor a Limit Trigger around something that a character can tangibly oppose or avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T08:31:08-07:00","id":1245496,"title":"","content":"I've been tempted to create a mechanism to trade Limit-gain for motes. Probably not even to tell the players unless I can really get them on the ropes in an extreme situation, and see if I can tempt them with power fueled by Limit. <br /> <br /> I'd want the story that came out of this kind of option to feel like suffering the indignity of a beat-down, but catching a second-wind and standing back up with an attitude of defiance, hate, frustration, etc. They'd need to play through the emotional fallout of such a Scene, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T08:46:59-07:00","id":1245503,"title":"","content":"How would that work in actual limit break though? It would feel weird for them to run out of steam just as they let loose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T09:28:17-07:00","id":1245517,"title":"","content":"In assessment of the Realm, at least in terms of its origins, I'd note that it's unlike any real life impetus for imperialism in that it formed in the aftermath of the world having very nearly ended. That defined both the environment that it existed in, and the motivations underlying its policies (which would have also been informed by the memory of the Shogunate). It's been my general read on the initial imperialism that it was compelled both by a sense that order needed to be imposed upon a chaotic Threshold (that would have also been vulnerable to Anathema), and that there needed to be a national grand strategy to give the Dragon Blooded something to do besides constantly fighting each other over territories under their direct control and access to the highest office in the land.<br /> <br /> So one could read the beginning of the Realm as founded in good intentions executed with ruthlessness. One can even play that as the motive that persisted throughout; that the Empress remained constantly alert for keeping the house of cards from collapsing, to the detriment of her personal peace of mind and self-interest (possibly to the point that she wound up largely desensitizing herself to the lives of others), and that was an attitude that she prioritized in her most highly placed ministers and personal agents; the likes of Bal Keraz and Tepet Eshana.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, the Realm itself runs into structural issues; you get Great Houses that become successful enough to raise flags for the Empress, ones that are still inclined for something well-intentioned but ruthless, with the ruthlessness to the point of entertaining bad decisions, ones whose appetites are growing past the point of sustainability, and some who still wound up having their own secret agendas of dubious quality.<br /> <br /> It can be an open question to the individual group as to whether the political landscape presented in What Fire Has Wrought is relatively unexceptional in the history of the Realm, the sort of thing that comes up every couple hundred years, the kinds of plates that the Empress had become well-practiced at spinning (possibly having started with an aptitude that would have been why Chejop supported her in the first place)\u2026 or if it's the kind of thing that the Realm had been building up to across the entire length of its existence, accumulating more and more issues until it becomes hard for it to not fall apart. One can develop different games from whether the absence of the Scarlet Empress is a cause or symptom of the current crisis.<br /> <br /> But as the place of the Realm in the setting goes, whether or not it's good or bad might matter less than the fact that it is in a position of desperation, both in whole and in parts. In particular, Houses Ledaal, Nellens, Tepet and V'neef have the demeanour of wounded animals, and that can make them dangerous and unpredictable.<br /> <br /> I've always liked the quote about the game of thrones being one that you either win or die, because I think it captures the mindset of a lot of dynastic or similar power struggles across history; where assessing a given figure's moral character becomes difficult when, for a number of reasons (not all of which are necessarily in their control), the question of who winds up in charge is literally one of life and death.<br /> <br /> Even if, in practical terms, winning does not always need to mean killing everybody else; just the fear that losing has a high enough chance of meaning death that it's unacceptable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T09:35:21-07:00","id":1245523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245503#post1245503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would that work in actual limit break though? It would feel weird for them to run out of steam just as they let loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reverse the order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My temptation is to stage a scene where they rise again from the brink of losing a battle, win the day, but suffer a Limit Break right after. <br /> <br /> For example, the Dawn warrior who is nearly pulled into the mouth of hell by the gibbering horde of demons his Circle is facing. He knows that if he falls, his Circle is doomed. In a fit of frustration and rage, he rises once more - empowered with a reserve of Motes - and strikes them down. After the battle, he's unable to stop lashing out, even to allies and underlings. He's reached a Limit Break and is in the grasp of his deliberate cruelty. <br /> <br /> That, to me, could be a really fun Scene to play through. The mechanical contrivance of motes-for-limit would merely enable that. The downside would be introducing a game mechanic for what, to me, should be a special turning point in a story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T09:54:33-07:00","id":1245535,"title":"","content":"This is a good thread, and I really liked reading all of y'all's opinions. I have, however, a radical thesis:<br /> <br /> <b>Sol and Luna are the bad guys. The Yozi are the good guys. The Exalted are rearranging deck chairs in the S.S. Titanic which is also parked in Stalingrad. </b><br /> <br /> Sorcerous Overlord, you daft fool! The Yozi are eviiiiiil! Perhaps, perhaps, but let's look at the facts. The Yozi are a collection of some few dozen eldritch abominations, which are places and concepts made real, that came from the &quot;everything and nothing LSD trip&quot; Chaos. They decided that this was tiresome, and so they made a reality of their own. Then, they made some beings to regulate Creation, and some even lesser beings to furnish them with adoration. Things managed themselves and two especially well made beings protected Creation from things that popped out of the Wyld and even held at bay from rival Yozi who wanted to break the snowglobe. Tired from their labor, they constructed the Games for themselves and everything went on safe and secure.<br /> <br /> The first beings did not like this arrangement, because they had to work and not play. so they wanted to kill their progenitors and steal the games like a bunch of traitorous jerks But the Yozi made them <i>literally incapable</i> of doing that, so they decided they'd toss some <i>god killing super power</i> into the lesser creations, and then arm them against their parent Yozi.<br /> <br /> These lesser beings got various flavors of god killing juice, and they killed a bunch of the Yozi, whose only crime was leaving Creation to perpetually run itself with 0% apocalypse chance. Half got killed, half got trapped in the <i>inside out surgery horror body of their king</i>. The First Beings took the games, the Yozi lead an existence of pure suffering, and the Least Beings moved up sorta into what the First Beings were supposed to do. Then the First Beings got lazy and ignored how bad the God Killers were, and just washed their hands of it.<br /> <br /> Then the weaker flavour god killers killed the stronger ones and locked them in a prison, and around this time it turns out that everyone forgot they were supposed to defend their snowglobe from the snowglobe eating, brick wielding monsters and a lot of Very Bad Globe Smashing happened. Admittedly, some of this snowglobe smashing happened from the Yozi who tried to take their ball and go home, but it was their ball that they made in the first place.<br /> <br /> Now the Weaker God Killer's Queen is missing and the Stronger God Killers are back and they are arguing about which of them is the better of the Lesser Beings. The gods still sit at the games faffing about, and the Snowglobe makers still suffer in eternity, but maybe some of them are trying to fix that.<br /> <br /> So Creation has had 2~5ish small apocalypses (which is a number more than 0), countless mortals have died needlessly (and the system they use to come back to life was broken too), and only fragments of a broken snowglobe remain.<br /> <br /> All because a few upstart gods wanted to Relax and Have Fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T10:02:37-07:00","id":1245540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245535#post1245535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have, however, a radical thesis:</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this an ironic throwback, or a genuine suggestion?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T10:34:16-07:00","id":1245548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245540#post1245540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this an ironic throwback, or a genuine suggestion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Though the manner I expressed myself in is humorous, I really do believe that the Yozi were unfairly wronged and people tend to just take it as a <i>de facto</i> truth that they had to go. For the common mortal, life under the Yozi was safer. No Deathlord Plague, no Baloran Crusade, no Universal retconning when then Yozi removed things from existence in their death-throes. All of the troubles now afflicting mortals are the result of the Gods wanting to sit at the Big Kids Table and causing the inevitable fuck ups thereafter. It's no coincidence that the Time of Sorrows is like the 4th case of &quot;And then the Lower overthrew the Higher and made everything less safe in the long term&quot;. Yozi-Gods-Solars-DBs(-thousand stream river humanity).<br /> <br /> Mortals got nothing out of this system, other than they are more free to die needlessly and be stuck as a tormented ghost so that .0001% of them can become Magic People With Really Good Lives as opposed to just Kings and Queens. They had a perpetual soul reincarnation system and everyone would have had a turn as a King or Merchant Lord or whatever. For the average farmer or laborer, they are now worse off and with no benefit. Just another serf exploited for the gain of their masters. There's no need for a Wyld Hunt or a Solar when creation was defended by Luna and Sol and their Anti-Chaos Super Group.<br /> <br /> I am a Yozi Supporter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T10:51:59-07:00","id":1245551,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://25.media.tumblr.com/b05ecea8f8fcdab469535638a1cd157a/tumblr_mf2lrp5uUx1rglcgso1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T11:01:35-07:00","id":1245554,"title":"","content":"interesting that you chose a well meaning but ultimately dangerous villain to make your point. Someone who has an idea about how they would fix everything if only they had power over everyone, and then fails, hurts innocents, and squanders their gain by becoming a petty tyrant.<br /> <br /> So yeah, thanks for agreeing with me. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T11:33:42-07:00","id":1245565,"title":"","content":"Uh... Where do you get the idea that mortals has a good life under the Yozi? <br /> <br /> Cause what I remember was that they basically treated mortals as insects beneath their notice, crushing, killing immolating etc without regard to humans in any way. Except y'know, the kind of Yozi that loved to pull the wings off of flies (the flies in this case are humans and the wings are limbs. Or souls.)<br /> <br /> Plus the Dragon Kings ritually sacrificed humans all the time. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure where, in any edition, you got the idea that humans were somehow less susceptible to random brutality and murder?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T11:35:08-07:00","id":1245567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245548#post1245548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though the manner I expressed myself in is humorous, I really do believe that the Yozi were unfairly wronged and people tend to just take it as a <i>de facto</i> truth that they had to go. For the common mortal, life under the Yozi was safer. No Deathlord Plague, no Baloran Crusade, no Universal retconning when then Yozi removed things from existence in their death-throes. All of the troubles now afflicting mortals are the result of the Gods wanting to sit at the Big Kids Table and causing the inevitable fuck ups thereafter. It's no coincidence that the Time of Sorrows is like the 4th case of &quot;And then the Lower overthrew the Higher and made everything less safe in the long term&quot;. Yozi-Gods-Solars-DBs(-thousand stream river humanity).<br /> <br /> Mortals got nothing out of this system, other than they are more free to die needlessly and be stuck as a tormented ghost so that .0001% of them can become Magic People With Really Good Lives as opposed to just Kings and Queens. They had a perpetual soul reincarnation system and everyone would have had a turn as a King or Merchant Lord or whatever. For the average farmer or laborer, they are now worse off and with no benefit. Just another serf exploited for the gain of their masters. There's no need for a Wyld Hunt or a Solar when creation was defended by Luna and Sol and their Anti-Chaos Super Group.<br /> <br /> I am a Yozi Supporter.</div> </div> </div> </div>going backwards:<br /> <br /> Your a Primodial Supporter. The Yozi's are the insane demon kings who are left after the Primodial's were crippled. No one wants Malfeas in charge, at least any version of him we've seen thus far.<br /> <br /> Did the Shogunate make the world less safe then the First Age? <i>ehhhh</i>, yes but in ways that the Dragonblooded were able to solve, albiet less elegantly. Fact of thte matter is...the DBs saved the day. Her Redness won. But yes, the shogunate was definetly 'less' then the first Age. Less 'safe' depends on if you think the First Age was nightmares start to finish, or not.<br /> <br /> Did the First Age make the world less safe then the 'Gods'? Not...not really. THere's no age of the gods rule/solar revolt against heaven (Although, maybe the sea war thing will be that?). I'm skipping this one.<br /> <br /> Did the Gods/Exalts make things safer then the primodials?...For who? For humans? I mean, they are allowed their own freedom and destiny, instead of being in nomine under Dragon King heel, and the capacity to become world shaping heroes, the undisputed most powerful group in creation next to the gods, and the wonderous golden age that was the first age. For non-human mortals? Probably worse, although there's no longer a black hole wandering around killing things by existing. So...Yeah. It's a bit of a stretch to say &quot;a dozen elder gods wandering around was a net gain for humanity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Buuuut, I hear you say, if we just kow towed to our inhuman masters and didn't fight back, we wouldn't have created the underworld. Funny thing. Regarding the Underworld pre-Divine Revolution:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1166419#post1166419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Underworld as we know it didn't exist, but that's not an answer of &quot;yes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think fundamentally, exalted has not pointed to &quot;The Higher are gone, so things are less safe.&quot; If anything, it's pointed to &quot;Lesser, but Safe.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T11:37:21-07:00","id":1245570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245548#post1245548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though the manner I expressed myself in is humorous, I really do believe that the Yozi were unfairly wronged and people tend to just take it as a <i>de facto</i> truth that they had to go. For the common mortal, life under the Yozi was safer. No Deathlord Plague, no Baloran Crusade, no Universal retconning when then Yozi removed things from existence in their death-throes. All of the troubles now afflicting mortals are the result of the Gods wanting to sit at the Big Kids Table and causing the inevitable fuck ups thereafter. It's no coincidence that the Time of Sorrows is like the 4th case of &quot;And then the Lower overthrew the Higher and made everything less safe in the long term&quot;. Yozi-Gods-Solars-DBs(-thousand stream river humanity).<br /> <br /> Mortals got nothing out of this system, other than they are more free to die needlessly and be stuck as a tormented ghost so that .0001% of them can become Magic People With Really Good Lives as opposed to just Kings and Queens. They had a perpetual soul reincarnation system and everyone would have had a turn as a King or Merchant Lord or whatever. For the average farmer or laborer, they are now worse off and with no benefit. Just another serf exploited for the gain of their masters. There's no need for a Wyld Hunt or a Solar when creation was defended by Luna and Sol and their Anti-Chaos Super Group.<br /> <br /> I am a Yozi Supporter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm Ishvara class Rhaksha still attacked Creation. Rhaksha in general still occaisonally went into Creation and fed on people. Not to mention that people in Creation don't really deal with those things listed on a daily basis. The Balorian Crusade and Great Contagion were singular events that by the current era its pretty much the same thing as the Black Death and World War 1. They were big, they were terrifying, people are probably worried about it happening again, and there are ripples in the world that are a side effect of it, but it isn't like elders can sit there and go, &quot;Bah, you call that a world ending plague? When I was your age we had six of those, and it didn't leave no stinking survivors in its wake just because monsters from beyond reality were unmaking existence. No the land rose up after it was killed. I watched a zombie mountain eat three of the elemental poles, you didn't even know we had.&quot; Also I don't think human in Creation even knows the Three Spheres Cataclysm was a thing, let alone something they have to deal with anymore than modern humans have to deal with the bit where the moon was likely carved out when a large meteor slammed into molten planet and caused molten rock to spin off.<br /> <br /> Its also not a particularly good argument for them being unfairly treated if one of the defenses you have is that no one would have had to deal the intense horrors that they unleashed when they lost. That's almost literally arguing that if a person was fired from their job for being an asshole and then they came back the next day and started just murdering everyone they could find that the person who fired the murderer is at fault because the murderer wouldn't have killed anyone otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T11:38:28-07:00","id":1245572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245548#post1245548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though the manner I expressed myself in is humorous, I really do believe that the Yozi were unfairly wronged and people tend to just take it as a <i>de facto</i> truth that they had to go. For the common mortal, life under the Yozi was safer. No Deathlord Plague, no Baloran Crusade, no Universal retconning when then Yozi removed things from existence in their death-throes. All of the troubles now afflicting mortals are the result of the Gods wanting to sit at the Big Kids Table and causing the inevitable fuck ups thereafter. It's no coincidence that the Time of Sorrows is like the 4th case of &quot;And then the Lower overthrew the Higher and made everything less safe in the long term&quot;. Yozi-Gods-Solars-DBs(-thousand stream river humanity).<br /> <br /> Mortals got nothing out of this system, other than they are more free to die needlessly and be stuck as a tormented ghost so that .0001% of them can become Magic People With Really Good Lives as opposed to just Kings and Queens. They had a perpetual soul reincarnation system and everyone would have had a turn as a King or Merchant Lord or whatever. For the average farmer or laborer, they are now worse off and with no benefit. Just another serf exploited for the gain of their masters. There's no need for a Wyld Hunt or a Solar when creation was defended by Luna and Sol and their Anti-Chaos Super Group.<br /> <br /> I am a Yozi Supporter.</div> </div> </div> </div>They literally used to be at the bottom of the food chain and slaves to dragon kings and this has been a thing since first edition. How humanity being in the worst place in prehistory make that better than this current situation? Like make no mistake the exalted have done horrible things but they're still in a better position than they were during prehistory. There's a reason why humanity had no problem with the yozi plan. Because fuck the yozi, they were horrible and alien.<br /> <br /> Also, the reason gods were working hard was because it was the primordial's playground and if they wanted to alter it, reshape it, or casually genocide races, they just did it. The gods had to work to maintain creation because the primordials did whatever the fuck they wanted and it couldn't sustain itself with that much pressure being put on the loom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 08-13-2018, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T12:02:43-07:00","id":1245585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the common mortal, life under the Yozi was safer </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Primordials are beings of immense and broad-reaching power who have basically no consideration for human lives, their whims and experimentation were terrible for humanity. Additionally, they had humans enslaved by Dragon Kings, who could be extremely brutal and ruthless.<br /> <br /> Primordials might be considered &quot;in the right&quot; in some ways, but as far as the life of humanity goes, you would have a hard time convincing me they had it better back then. Reminder that Primordials made humans as frail as they are to begin with, when they clearly can make things with Behemoth-level immortality, so tell me who made human lives less safe?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T12:12:12-07:00","id":1245588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245585#post1245585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Primordials are beings of immense and broad-reaching power who have basically no consideration for human lives, their whims and experimentation were terrible for humanity. Additionally, they had humans enslaved by Dragon Kings, who could be extremely brutal and ruthless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd characterize the Dragon Kings as more careless and callous than anything else. They also paid a steep price for it when the enemies of the gods killed tens of millions of them for keeps<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Primordials might be considered &quot;in the right&quot; in some ways, but as far as the life of humanity goes, you would have a hard time convincing me they had it better back then. Reminder that Primordials made humans as frail as they are to begin with, when they clearly can make things with Behemoth-level immortality, so tell me who made human lives less safe? </div> </div> </div>The Yozis were even more callous than the Dragon Kings, and arguably got off light if they didn't become Neverborn. Also, I don't think that we're going with the &quot;intentionally created humans to be weaker, easily-scared Mountain Folk&quot; in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T12:58:06-07:00","id":1245609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245570#post1245570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's almost literally arguing that if a person was fired from their job for being an asshole and then they came back the next day and started just murdering everyone they could find that the person who fired the murderer is at fault because the murderer wouldn't have killed anyone otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it much differently than you do. To me, it's like saying &quot;I can't believe that when we broke into this lady's house to steal the deed and murder her she had the gall to kick over a lantern and set the place on fire. The nerve of some people&quot;.<br /> <br /> To the others: I'm glad we're moving the discussion!<i> Let the hate flow through you...</i> In no order- Are the Yozi responsible for the Dragon Kings treatment of Humanity? Are humans enslaved by the Guild and enserfed by the Realm better off, or is this a pro-human justification? Do we treat humanity as a &quot;kinder, gentler machine gun hand&quot;? What counter argument rebukes the claim that the UCS and Luna for abandoned their jobs for petty reasons? Why are we letting the UCS, Luna et al. off the hook for ignoring the conditions of the Decline of the First Age? They are as much to blame as anyone for turning their backs on their progeny's suffering- <i>the very crime the Primordials are accused of</i>. Nothing changed on their end. They could have smashed the Jade Prison. Sol Invictus appears to most Zeniths and basically no one else- what the malfeas is he so busy doing? He's on a crack binge and can't be bothered to fix anything.<br /> <br /> What evidence do we have that Apocalypses great and small are a better deal than the yoke of the Primordials? Remember when XenoPrimordial got jealous of Creation and tried to make his own and join it with ours, and the Primordials stopped him with an Infinity Canon? What if he came back tomorrow? Who's got that level of power- The Scarlet Empress and the Realm Defense Grid? No, the Lunars were right- Creation <b>cannot</b> defend itself. Every step of the whole bloody history has been sacrificing long term security for short term power grabs.<br /> <br /> Collectively, the fandom has always jumped passed &quot;Overthrowing the Primordials was justified&quot; so they could argue if &quot;the Usurpation was justified&quot;. Hell, we call killing the the Solars <i>The Usurpation </i>but killing the Primordials <i>the Primordial War</i>. It was the original Usurpation! And what did humanity get, meet the new boss, same as the old boss. It such an interesting period with fascinating ramifications- but it's consigned to the &quot;Time Of Myth&quot; so we can get into the Story Proper.<br /> <br /> And on another note, vis-a-vis the terrible no good dirty rotten Dragon Kings: are they bad because they <b>enslaved </b>humans, or are they bad because they enslaved <b>humans</b>? Because if it's the latter we have to concede that morality doesn't matter, only speciesism matters. There's plenty of Human on Human slavery, murder, torture, experimentation going on in the Age of Sorrows, except its being done by factions we get to play as.<br /> <br /> ... you know, I think I'm becoming an Infernal. Why do I have a PM from Gorol?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T13:18:22-07:00","id":1245614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see it much differently than you do. To me, it's like saying &quot;I can't believe that when we broke into this lady's house to steal the deed and murder her she had the gall to kick over a lantern and set the place on fire. The nerve of some people&quot;.<br /> <br /> To the others: I'm glad we're moving the discussion!<i> Let the hate flow through you...</i> In no order- Are the Yozi responsible for the Dragon Kings treatment of Humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They created humans. They created the Dragon kings. They told the Dragon kings that they were in charge of the humans<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are humans enslaved by the Guild and enserfed by the Realm better off, or is this a pro-human justification?</div> </div> </div> </div>A better way to ask this is: Are some of humanity being enslaved better than all of humanity and every other creature great and small? So yes. <br /> <br /> Even if you just focus on those enslaved by the guild, those people are still property. Property cannot be sold if you destroy it. Which is infinitely better than 'insects' to be exterminated, experimented on or played with at the Yozi's whim because they just. didn't. care.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we treat humanity as a &quot;kinder, gentler machine gun hand&quot;? What counter argument rebukes the claim that the UCS and Luna for abandoned their jobs for petty reasons?</div> </div> </div> </div>UCS and Luna regard their jobs much as former slaves regard their previous 'duties' because they were also slaves to the Yozi.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are we letting the UCS, Luna et al. off the hook for ignoring the conditions of the Decline of the First Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is somewhat of an existential question. It boils down to 'free will' <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are as much to blame as anyone for turning their backs on their progeny's suffering- <i>the very crime the Primordials are accused of</i>. Nothing changed on their end. They could have smashed the Jade Prison. Sol Invictus appears to most Zeniths and basically no one else- what the malfeas is he so busy doing? He's on a crack binge and can't be bothered to fix anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>They gave humanity the reigns. As the ancient saying goes &quot;No take-backsies&quot; <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What evidence do we have that Apocalypses great and small are a better deal than the yoke of the Primordials? Remember when XenoPrimordial got jealous of Creation and tried to make his own and join it with ours, and the Primordials stopped him with an Infinity Canon? What if he came back tomorrow? Who's got that level of power- The Scarlet Empress and the Realm Defense Grid? No, the Lunars were right- Creation <b>cannot</b> defend itself. Every step of the whole bloody history has been sacrificing long term security for short term power grabs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because to humanity and the rest of the creatures at the bottom of the totem pole cataclysms happened ALL THE TIME. Oh you're living in Great Forks? Sorry, Cecelyne decided it would be a great place for a summer palace and she murdered hundreds of thousands of people who lived there. She didn't notice that they lived there any more than you would notice the thousands of ants that you massacre every time we, as humans, construct a building. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Collectively, the fandom has always jumped passed &quot;Overthrowing the Primordials was justified&quot; so they could argue if &quot;the Usurpation was justified&quot;. Hell, we call killing the the Solars <i>The Usurpation </i>but killing the Primordials <i>the Primordial War</i>. It was the original Usurpation! And what did humanity get, meet the new boss, same as the old boss. It such an interesting period with fascinating ramifications- but it's consigned to the &quot;Time Of Myth&quot; so we can get into the Story Proper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, WHERE do you get the idea that life under the exalted has EVER been even close to life under the primordials? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on another note, vis-a-vis the terrible no good dirty rotten Dragon Kings: are they bad because they <b>enslaved </b>humans, or are they bad because they enslaved <b>humans</b>? Because if it's the latter we have to concede that morality doesn't matter, only speciesism matters. There's plenty of Human on Human slavery, murder, torture, experimentation going on in the Age of Sorrows, except its being done by factions we get to play as.</div> </div> </div> </div>pretty sure it was the thousands of sentient people that they enslaved and ritually murdered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T13:23:19-07:00","id":1245617,"title":"","content":"The problem with an argument over the Primordial War is that it's impossible to evaluate.<br /> <br /> I mean, quite literally so in 1st and 2nd edition. It's explicit canon that nobody in the setting knows what was lost when She Who Lives In Her Name's sphere-cracking exercise went through. So what could have been obliterated were terrible horrors that made human life utter misery by later standards . . . or great blessings against which even the beneficiaries of the highest wonders of the First Age were living in wretched misery by pre-War standards. It's <i>canon</i> that you can't actually compare conditions before and after the Primordial War, so you can't actually evaluate whether it was better or worse.<br /> <br /> In 3rd edition, on the other hand, we have so little canon at all on anything that happened so long ago, as a matter of developer policy, that it's similarly impossible to compare conditions before and after. (Go ahead and try, giving cites to the actual page numbers in 3rd edition books where you get you data on conditions in the Time Before or First Age.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T13:33:36-07:00","id":1245620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see it much differently than you do. To me, it's like saying &quot;I can't believe that when we broke into this lady's house to steal the deed and murder her she had the gall to kick over a lantern and set the place on fire. The nerve of some people&quot;.<br /> <br /> What evidence do we have that Apocalypses great and small are a better deal than the yoke of the Primordials? Remember when XenoPrimordial got jealous of Creation and tried to make his own and join it with ours, and the Primordials stopped him with an Infinity Canon? What if he came back tomorrow? Who's got that level of power- The Scarlet Empress and the Realm Defense Grid? No, the Lunars were right- Creation <b>cannot</b> defend itself. Every step of the whole bloody history has been sacrificing long term security for short term power grabs.</div> </div> </div> </div>...the doom canon's still around. he's playing checkers, and seems pretty sure the mortals can handle thier problems, which has been accurate so far. Like. The Infinity Canon is <i>right there</i>. <i>He just decided to do things again. </i><br /> Also I'd be suprised to see &quot;XenoPrimodial&quot; be a thing anymore, kinda for this reason. Primodial War is over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245609#post1245609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Collectively, the fandom has always jumped passed &quot;Overthrowing the Primordials was justified&quot; so they could argue if &quot;the Usurpation was justified&quot;. Hell, we call killing the the Solars <i>The Usurpation </i>but killing the Primordials <i>the Primordial War</i>. It was the original Usurpation! And what did humanity get, meet the new boss, same as the old boss. It such an interesting period with fascinating ramifications- but it's consigned to the &quot;Time Of Myth&quot; so we can get into the Story Proper.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, welomce to &quot;we overthrew the hostile beings of creation so humanity could foster--oh they were beuatiful, awe inspiring, and majestic, but they need to die&quot;. Also in the party is Leviathan, Tiamat (Hell, Marduk's <i>perfect</i> for your complaints. Humans <i>are</i> slaves in that one, and ancient standards never held Tiamat as sympathetic. She's was an awful creature that lost--and was replaced by a better king who by today's standards is still an ego centric king), 7Macaw( well, more his 2 kids who kept making and destroying mountains but whatever), Kronos/Uranos (Again, Kronos has a great case if your roman! Where he supposedly ruled a golden age as Saturn, but still, he ate his kids. Uranos needed to be seperated to allow humanity to flourish, no matter how much he loved his wife), Ymir, and <i>more.</i> <br /> Humanity didn't flourish and reach it's Zenith under the rulership of the wandering elder gods...they did it under the rule of the Exalted Host. The First Age <i>is</i> the Golden age, even if it eventually descended into an Age of Nightmares. And I love the idea of an Age of Nightmares, but the First Age was a time of wonders unheard of and unseen since, that benefited all humanity in the way mythic golden ages always do. Or, in other words, it took 2 more apoclypses and the decline of the First Age for humanity to reach a new boss arguably the same as the old boss (Arguably--I suspect &quot;Primodial got bored in your village&quot; is much worse then &quot;the Dynast got bored in your village&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T16:56:45-07:00","id":1245682,"title":"","content":"So Primordial War. Since we've gone there as is inevitable in these sorts of threads. It was pretty tenable in First Edition, at least for most of the edition, that the Primordial War could be argued to be a Bad Idea or at least unjustified. It was not well defined how much the Primordials of the age were actively malevolent towards life in the world, or how much the kind of chaotic, fecund magic they brought into the world could be mitigated, or how much the rebellion by the Incarna was a power grab, or how much the Primordials were changed into much worse beings by death and suffering. The First Edition writers and developers mostly didn't want to get into it - I can't remember if Geoff Grabowski ever commented on the subject.<br /> <br /> From late 1e to 2e, you mostly had Neph and then Holden, who did hold, in contrast, strong public views that the Primordial War should and must be justified and the Incarna should to a degree be in the right, with their thumb on the scale of how sadistic and malevolent and dangerous the Primordials would be. And so it would become increasingly difficult to argue any alternative.<br /> <br /> 3e, which was again initially at least under Holden's direction, walked away somewhat from the idea that it's something that the books should get into, rather than a distraction from the human focused drama of the Age of Sorrows. (Though I think he still would've answered &quot;Fuck the Primordials&quot; if you ever asked him!).<br /> <br /> So it's one of those things I would have been up for arguing about in the (increasingly distant) past, but kind of not anymore because either you come to the conclusion of 1) if you use most of the pre-Holden+Neph material, we really don't and can't know, or 2) no, if you use most of the canon, the Primordials were clearly in the wrong... but that's doesn't seem very interesting either because it mostly just reflects Ascended Fans solving arguments they got involved in on the internet in favour of their preference, once they were in control of the canon. (Like, if we were having this thread' discussion about whether the Dragonblooded could be &quot;the good guys&quot; and then a fan who felt very vehemently that they shouldn't ever be, got into control of the canon and wrote it such that they couldn't be, you'd have to admit that the argument was &quot;solved&quot;... but I don't think you'd feel very enthusiastic about it.)<br /> <br /> (This is admittedly totally a kind of third wall breaking, mostly useless for people who just want to get into the heads of the setting kind of argument, and probably kind of repellent for new people who are not interested in all these shifts and view clashes over time, which are now, what ten years dead. Just kind of hard for me to look at through another perspective I guess.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T22:58:40-07:00","id":1245771,"title":"","content":"I do think its arguable that the Primordial War isn't relevant; the Yozis *now* are incompatible with a happy and healthy life in Creation. I do like it as a twisted mirror of the Ursurpation with the difference being Solars are humans, who try and fail and learn and can be BETTER this time around, whereas the Primordials were vast and alien beings who didn't have failure as a concept, only disagreement, and the world not perfectly responding to their wishes broke them more than mere imprisonment did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T01:06:05-07:00","id":1245792,"title":"","content":"{watching thread disappear down the rabbit hole of Yozi Advocacy arguments}<br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/villains/images/5/5d/Joanna_goodbye.gif/revision/latest?cb=20170512195520\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Now Joanna, don't be so harsh! I, for one, welcome the hard left turn, out of freaking nowhere, away from discussion of the ethical considerations of the Realm and the variety of personalities therein, into the subject of the moral implications of ancient Ymir slaying mythology and arguing the perspective of the Flying Spaghetti Monster. <br /> <br /> Truth be told, I was growing bored of the complexities and intricacies of individual and national motivations underlying imperialist policies, and the manner in which that constrains and defines the manner in which the morality of human characters, that are actually active and significant in the timeframe of the game, can not only develop, but can be effectively expressed. And the resonance it has with actual social issues of today, of how one can reconcile one's self-perception with engagement with states that may very well have dubious domestic and foreign policies, or dealing with the inability to have ethical consumption under capitalism, that was all getting a bit too real for me.<br /> <br /> Nono, we're much better off with the question of &quot;what if the Devil had a point, maaaaaaaaaaaaaajhdhdjjsjhadajahshshhSnSHHDH<span style=\"font-size:18px\">J</span><span style=\"font-size:8px\">H</span><span style=\"font-size:20px\">D</span><span style=\"font-size:8px\">KjD</span><span style=\"font-size:24px\">jfo</span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">iPn</span>Krn<span style=\"font-size:18px\">D</span>Hfv<span style=\"font-size:11px\">vb</span>tcvd------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ooof, sorry; must have been some kind of technical error.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T05:42:14-07:00","id":1245835,"title":"","content":"Isator, hey, you could not start a new thread and perhaps some of us'll dip our toes?<br /> <br /> Though I did want to comment on your point from #45 about how the Realm formed in a response to an impetus that is unparalleled in real world history. I'd agree with it quite a bit, but also challenge that a little, that there may be more RW common ground - there are certainly shades of the unification of China. <br /> <br /> The Realm is put together with a conscious idea of historical cultural unity, the Old Realm, after a period of &quot;Warring States&quot; nominally under unity under the Shogun, with some justification of being in order to oppose an external foe (the Fae in the case of the Realm), and preserve the unified ideal of civilization. So potentially parallels with Chinese unification here (the Shang and Zhou are the idealized Old Realm, powerful dangerous Mongolic steppe competitors are like the Fae, at least as experienced by the frontier Qin state). Though not Roman unification of the Mediterranean (which is not any sense a &quot;re-unification&quot; even ideologically to its founders).<br /> <br /> (Of course, I'm being a bit loose in applying some factors here, like the degree to which they'd actually experienced a massive invasion).<br /> <br /> At the other end in terms of how the Realm operates in the Threshold and much of the world, the better available analogy for the Realm *is* probably Rome around the Mediterranean. There you have a clear central power which does extract by tax from the periphery of its empire to fund spending by its governors, military and in its core. Rome does hold these territories because they are launching pads for barbarian invasion and competitor states (e.g. analogously, anathema led assaults for the Realm) , yet are not integrated under a shared memory of cultural unity. Rebellions are frequent. At the same time, despite all this extraction, the effect of unified governance and the &quot;Pax Romana&quot; (despite significant warfare from rebellions) maybe really does boost trade and productivity and how people (at least some) live all around the Mediterranean and not just in Italy.<br /> <br /> (What doesn't apply so well to my mind is mostly European colonialism in the &quot;New World&quot;, or in its two phases (Early Modern and 19th century) in Asia and Africa. Or the recent world system and international global capitalism. These all being characterized by economic systems, technologies, circumstances, histories, social changes and balances of power that mostly don't exist in the Realm's encounter with the rest of the world. There are bits that apply, and in some places more applies, but the enabling and spurring factors and practices mostly seem more different. But that's a topic and tangent probably for another thread.)<br /> <br /> On your wider post there, I have less to comment, I'm think maybe less sympathetic to the idea that the Realm is under anything like a rational strategy (&quot;national grand strategy&quot;) to constrain and channel the Dragon Blooded to useful ends, rather than formed through exigency and to maintain power in the short term (across a lot of successive short terms!), and to manage recurrent crises.<br /> <br /> All that said, the Realm would seem to face many more constraints than even the analogous real world empires in selecting a new elite that is chosen for loyalty to the state and the nation beyond aristocratic loyalties. Chinese dynasties are able to slowly over time select talented people from gentry classes to replace dependence on elite aristocracy. The Realm probably can't really do anything like this so effectively, both because of the realities that the most talented individuals will be Dragonblooded Dynasts and because its religious system completely moves in the opposite direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T06:23:45-07:00","id":1245853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245835#post1245835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that said, the Realm would seem to face many more constraints than even the analogous real world empires in selecting a new elite that is chosen for loyalty to the state and the nation beyond aristocratic loyalties. Chinese dynasties are able to slowly over time select talented people from gentry classes to replace dependence on elite aristocracy. The Realm probably can't really do anything like this so effectively, both because of the realities that the most talented individuals will be Dragonblooded Dynasts and because its religious system completely moves in the opposite direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about lost eggs and outcastes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T06:32:06-07:00","id":1245856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245835#post1245835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Realm is put together with a conscious idea of historical cultural unity, the Old Realm, after a period of &quot;Warring States&quot; nominally under unity under the Shogun, with some justification of being in order to oppose an external foe (the Fae in the case of the Realm), and preserve the unified ideal of civilization. So potentially parallels with Chinese unification here (the Shang and Zhou are the idealized Old Realm, powerful dangerous Mongolic steppe competitors are like the Fae, at least as experienced by the frontier Qin state).</div> </div> </div> </div>That can be kind of analogous, but I'd still say falls far short.<br /> <br /> There have been events in history that have entailed some kind of major death and destruction that, to the people experiencing them, probably would have been severely traumatic or had something known and familiar torn away forever, or made it feel (literally or figuratively) like the world was ending. The Bronze Age collapse, the Black Death, 9/11... those can give a starting point for what the experience of the world in the days following the end of the Scarlet Empress using the Sword of Creation was like, but I would still say that something needs to expand beyond them. It all needs to come from the idea that in the Great Contagion and Fair Folk invasion, the majority of people died, and large parts of the world stopped existing.<br /> <br /> Set aside the likelihood that many people were in a state where, just days previously, they had been resigned to the probability that nothing could save them; think about what it's like for the known and the familiar to be so utterly torn away like that, the sheer enormity of the idea that most people who existed just a few years ago were now gone. The loss of land alone has enormous implications, cultural and economic; that's not a country being gone in the sense of a political transition; that's entire places, whole landscapes, that simply don't exist anymore. Even if they're not places that you ever personally visited before, or expected to ever visit, think about what it would be like to know that they don't exist anymore; nothing that came from there will ever come again, whole identities just dissolved in a flash.<br /> <br /> The game has never been wholly consistent on how much of Creation was lost to the Wyld (as opposed to its remains being greatly depopulated), but I honestly don't think that it would need to be very much to severely mess people up for quite a while.<br /> <br /> That's the world in which the Realm was formed; one in which there really had been, undeniably, unambiguously, devoid of all political rhetoric, a crisis of all-encompassing scale that had threatened not only &quot;civilization&quot;, but the existence of everything.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, one cannot reasonably assume that any of the actors involved would have had anything like objectivity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm think maybe less sympathetic to the idea that the Realm is under anything like a rational strategy (&quot;national grand strategy&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Grand strategy is just the technical term to refer to how a certain body (often a state) employs all of the resources at its command to achieve a defined long-term goal. It doesn't necessarily represent a value judgement on the plan or goal in question, nor does it imply one single plan that is rigidly adhered to at all stages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">to constrain and channel the Dragon Blooded to useful ends, rather than formed through exigency and to maintain power in the short term (across a lot of successive short terms!), and to manage recurrent crises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, how long is the short term in this case, and if it was only short term, what was the intention for afterwards?<br /> <br /> Again, this isn't about talking about a singular master plan, so much as a primary objective and the continuous development of secondary objectives in support of that, and plans in pursuit of the secondary objectives.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Realm, the idea that the Dragon Blooded have to be cultivated in accordance with policies that will keep them from disastrously fighting one another while still being available to contribute to an overall well-being is... something that I would imagine as just being a secondary objective, but one that takes a lot of priority.<br /> <br /> But it is something that I would see as a unifying thread in how the Scarlet Dynasty came into existence and how it functions, even if I would never frame it as something that adheres wholly to the vision of the Empress (itself an already fallible thing); it still noticeably consists of compromises, patches and ad hoc solutions. And whether or not it could have lasted much longer is an up-in-the-air question to explore in game.<br /> <br /> But I find the presentation of it as a system that would keep the Exalted from being like they were written as during the Shogunate to be plausible and compelling. More than that, I would find settling upon an underlying motivation of keeping the Dragon Blooded both satisfied and occupied, in pursuits that they can't openly fight one another over, to be a good basis for developing consistent backstory that can be used for many games involving the Dynasts and the Realm.<br /> <br /> It's at least something that I would find to resonate with several historical instances, such as Louis XIV being agreed upon to have developed the Versailles court culture as a way of occupying the highest aristocracy, or Toyotomi Hideyoshi's invasions of Korea being driven at least partially by a desire to direct the military ruling class of a newly unified nation collectively against an external foe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T06:49:56-07:00","id":1245859,"title":"","content":"So often, these posts follow the pattern:<br /> OP: &quot;Is this group at fault for this action?&quot;<br /> Response: &quot;Collective action is a myth. There are no groups, only individuals. And, are these individuals really at fault for their actions, when prior actors/destiny forced their hands? What is causality anyway?&quot;<br /> <br /> I think this is disingenuous. Yes, collective action is not only real, but evidenced (repeatedly) in the Exalted lore. Being good at collective action is arguably one of the Dragon-Blooded's shticks. Escaping destiny is also possible, which means you own the consequences of those actions (even if 'you' is a prior Exaltation that sided with the Unconquered Sun's revolt and brought the Great Curse upon your collective heads - the setting has a deliberate blur on Celestial identity). <br /> <br /> What we shouldn't jump to is collective punishment. Yes, the Dragon-Blooded may be responsible for a rapacious empire, and strongman dictatorships in the Threshold. Yes, perhaps that empire and those strongmen should be reformed or resisted, perhaps even violently. But you should fight the war with an eye on the peace. The surviving Dragon-Blooded will need a place in the new world order, and for that they must be forgiven for the crimes of their families, or even their own crimes. Be magnanimous in victory. The Unconquered Sun would expect nothing less of you.<br /> <br /> In this view, the Wyld Hunt is unjust cowardice. Unable to evaluate Anathema on their individual merits (even Fae. Even ghosts. Even demons.) the Sidereals have maneuvered the Dragon-Blooded into a kill on sight regime. While I respect the writers including it as a way to drive conflict in the setting, I don't respect it as an upright and moral way to engage your fellow sentient being. It is a policy for viruses or bacteria, not those capable of reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T07:03:20-07:00","id":1245865,"title":"","content":"While I agree about the rapacious Empire, when only about half the DBs in the world live there, I cannot see how you can blame all of them for it (regardless of whether you don't punish them for it). Lookshyans are not responsible for the Realm, nor are Outcastes.<br /> You can say the Scarlet Dynasty as a whole is responsible for the Empire, but it simply has nothing to do with, say, Outcaste Champions in the Hundred Kingdoms, or the Dragonblood admiral of Wavecrest, or a family of Dragonblood exorcists in the far north-west, etc.<br /> <br /> Nor, honestly, are nations in the Threshold with Dragonblood families particularly more dictatorial than those not with Dragonblood families. Lookshy isn't a lovely place, but it's a better place to live for normal people than many other cities.<br /> The problem is the Scarlet Dynasty, not the Dragonblood as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-14-2018, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T07:06:50-07:00","id":1245868,"title":"","content":"There's something to be said for how the common image of Anathema is not defined by Solars, but by the Lunars, and that the current setting is going with the idea that many of them have been acting in a manner consistent with the narrative of them being terrifying monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T07:09:41-07:00","id":1245869,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if the persecution of the wyld hunt drives some lunars to become the very monsters that it seeks to eradicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T07:10:12-07:00","id":1245870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245868#post1245868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something to be said for how the common image of Anathema is not defined by Solars, but by the Lunars, and that the current setting is going with the idea that many of them have been acting in a manner consistent with the narrative of them being terrifying monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose eating people, then using their shapes to infiltrate as well as deadly beastmen technique did them no favours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T07:17:43-07:00","id":1245874,"title":"","content":"Edit: I said something about how Isator is right about the medium-term irrelevance of Solars, and the gameline should remember this more, but this doesn't contradict the point about how killing Lunars indiscriminately is wrong, but then I realised I'm not invested enough in this to argue on one side or the other so I deleted it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-14-2018, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T07:54:49-07:00","id":1245878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245865#post1245865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when only about half the DBs in the world live there, I cannot see how you can blame all of them for it (regardless of whether you don't punish them for it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was attempting to blame the Dragon-Blooded for the governing methodology of dictatorship found throughout Creation. But, if you're hung up on it, substitute 'Dynasty' for 'Dragon-Blooded' and a lesser version of the point still stands, as I think you see with your next sentence. They, the Scarlet Dynasty, are collectively at fault for an empire's sins, and responsible for its accomplishments (including the continued existence of Creation).<br /> <br /> They are at fault in a way the Alchemicals are not, who have ceded political control to humanity and occupy a position as champions of a state they do not helm. Notably, the Alchemicals can still claim comparable accomplishments (the continued functioning of the Realm of Brass and Shadow).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:12:36-07:00","id":1245884,"title":"","content":"Well, Personally I do see them as good guys, and portray them as so. Sure some of them are corrupted bureaucrats and soldiers but not ALL of them.<br /> Most of them just want to make creation a safe place for everyone, even the empress. She tried to keep the whole world together however she could, sure, she had to make some very ''evil'' decisions, because she isn't as powerful as a celestial and her exaltation wasn't designed to rule, but despite everything she saved the world and kept it together. So yes, in my book, DBs are good guys. Specially the ones in the realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-14-2018, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:16:09-07:00","id":1245886,"title":"","content":"<i>None</i> of the exaltations were designed to rule. They were designed to be warriors and generals, not rulers.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons they're all so shit at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:22:26-07:00","id":1245888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245884#post1245884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> her exaltation wasn't designed to rule</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate this being a thought process still. It isn't true in 3e, at the least. DB have been leaders and rulers of humanity since time immemorial, in the ancient days founding dynasties that clashed with the early Solars and some even persisted on their own terms. Terrestrial Exalted are not born to be any Solar's assumed servant or soldier for the REAL rulers any more than Lunars are. Solars just are the best at whatever they go about doing because that's how they roll. Material difference I think.<br /> <br /> Or not and I just refuted my own argument? It made sense to me at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:26:01-07:00","id":1245889,"title":"","content":"It makes sense. <br /> <br /> Exaltations aren't designed to serve. Or rule. <br /> <br /> Exaltations are meant to amplify natural human prowess, skill, and action, to superhuman levels and effect, through the lens of the exaltations patron. <br /> <br /> Dragonblooded? Elemental effects. Fire, water, cooperation etc.<br /> <br /> Solars? Yellow energy constructs. Holy effects. Perfection. Amplification of base skill to supreme levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:41:42-07:00","id":1245893,"title":"","content":"I like how you listed &quot;yellow energy constructs&quot; first.<br /> <br /> Truly, the primary theme of the lawgivers is creating the iconic Glorious Solar Desk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:20:42-07:00","id":1245910,"title":"","content":"Don't forget Glorious Solar Bicycles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:21:58-07:00","id":1245912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245878#post1245878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was attempting to blame the Dragon-Blooded for the governing methodology of dictatorship found throughout Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure the Perfect of Paragon was thinking of using the Scarlet Dynasty as a model when he assumed his reign, not least because he is older than it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:46:12-07:00","id":1245925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245912#post1245912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure the Perfect of Paragon was thinking of using the Scarlet Dynasty as a model when he assumed his reign, not least because he is older than it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's being kind of pedantic at best. The Perfect strikes me as being a very good example of the kind of local autocrat that the Realm has a tendency to support with the perception that doing so more effectively sustains their policy in the Threshold.<br /> <br /> I think Tikor makes a good point; that an assessment of moral underpinnings to the supposed goal of preserving stability and security in the Threshold needs to be weighed against the chosen method of doing so being a model of dependence on the centre and supporting autocracies, that might be alternately seen as making life for common people under the system more miserable than necessary, and actually less stable than they might seem due to the problems of autocracy such as inflexibility or difficulties with adaptation (such as to the sudden death of the autocrat).<br /> <br /> Hmm... I'm suddenly having a brief flash of something that I read once about imperialism in ancient Anatolia, which was either from the policies of Greek or Persian expansion, and... might have taken the form of the imperialistic power attempting to exert power through appointing parliamentary bodies, that the local populaces rejected in favour of Tyrants?<br /> <br /> Nooo, I don't remember that subject well enough to take it into consideration here. For the time being, I'll agree that there's validity to the position that the measures the Realm takes with its satrapies are ultimately just a half-measure, and that they ought to be accountable for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:52:38-07:00","id":1245930,"title":"","content":"Is he? I don't think he's that old. I thought he was like 300.<br /> But anyway, history shows that dictatorship (including monarchy) is a pretty common way of ruling a country. We never had the Scarlet Dynasty in the real world, yet for most of history, most people were ruled by either central dictators, or local chiefs.<br /> In the Middle Ages, they looked back to Rome as being the greatest Empire ever, yet very few medieval Europeans created Republics like the Roman Republic.<br /> Having the example of a giant centralised state under one monarch is a good encouragement for others to do the same, yet I don't think it's the primary reason they exist. Central and South Americans had never heard of China, or Rome, or Alexander the Great, yet the Mexica, Inca, etc, still had a central ruler (who of course, was not identical to European monarchs, but then, they weren't identical to each other anyway).<br /> <br /> So, while I do agree that the Scarlet Dynasty is bad (and I feel it's not of little importance to differentiate that from Dragonblood, I think it's very important, just as you can't judge the Gold Faction by the Bronze Faction), I don't think it's their fault that Wavecrest is ruled by the Feathered One, or Skullstone is ruled by the Silver Prince, or Gem is ruled by the Despot, or as Alucard said, Paragon is ruled by the Perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:30:05-07:00","id":1245953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245886#post1245886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>None</i> of the exaltations were designed to rule. They were designed to be warriors and generals, not rulers.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons they're all so shit at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I mean, the Solars sure did a bang-up job of ruling the world during the Era of Nightmares, right? Ultimately despite their power all of the Exalted are human and they can still make mistakes, fuck up, be tyrants, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:35:53-07:00","id":1245955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245886#post1245886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>None</i> of the exaltations were designed to rule. They were designed to be warriors and generals, not rulers.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons they're all so shit at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken lol.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245888#post1245888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate this being a thought process still. It isn't true in 3e, at the least. DB have been leaders and rulers of humanity since time immemorial, in the ancient days founding dynasties that clashed with the early Solars and some even persisted on their own terms. Terrestrial Exalted are not born to be any Solar's assumed servant or soldier for the REAL rulers any more than Lunars are. Solars just are the best at whatever they go about doing because that's how they roll. Material difference I think.<br /> <br /> Or not and I just refuted my own argument? It made sense to me at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is material differences.Then again, you would assume that the chosens of the god of perfection would be better at leading than others.<br /> That's also why I added she wasn't that powerful as the celestial, not better ruler than them.<br /> It's kinda of an strategic RPG way of thinking, when you don't have enough resources you have to make choices about what to sacrifice to get things done. Same thing happen to her, being resources = to power.<br /> <br /> And seriously can one make a comment here without having an argument about which edition is better ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-14-2018, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:49:31-07:00","id":1245962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245955#post1245955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is material differences.Then again, you would assume that the chosens of the god of perfection would be better at leading than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not, actually. There's no Ability for being <i>good</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:01:06-07:00","id":1245968,"title":"","content":"Okay, the question of how representative or participatory various governments would be in their own right issssummm complicated. In character, one can probably at least have grievances based on the fact that the Realm promotes and enables activities that direct the resources of the land and its people for the benefit of the Realm, generally at the expense of the locals. Something like what was going on in the backstory of Perfect Soul; her family felt it was necessary to take extreme measures to remove dissidents, and then Mnemon came in to dig up their heritage and take a direct hand in crushing anybody that would protest that anyway, and what was the point of it all.<br /> <br /> They probably wouldn't express it in the terms that I have because a lot of them are educated differently, but it can still form a basis for opposition.<br /> <br /> That being said, following what I think was that example in Anatolia, it would be interesting if there was a satrapy in which the Realm instituted a form of government that was... probably not democratic, but at least in the form of a multi-part council, and there was dissatisfaction with it for some reason such as it being highly fractious by design, or just a means of giving direct authority to oligarchs in concert*, and the people kind of want something more direct and singular, if not an outright populist strongman.<br /> <br /> * Something that I've often found to render the conflation of pre-modern monarchs with modern dictators to be simplistic at best is that from what I can see, historically, monarchs have often been at odds with and prone to restraining the excesses of the landed upper classes, in a manner that at least incidentally benefited regular people, and in some cases even outright functioned as an authority to which commoners could appeal that would be over the head of local authorities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:20:00-07:00","id":1245980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245930#post1245930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Middle Ages, they looked back to Rome as being the greatest Empire ever, yet very few medieval Europeans created Republics like the Roman Republic.<br /> Having the example of a giant centralised state under one monarch is a good encouragement for others to do the same, yet I don't think it's the primary reason they exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know; I've heard Rome's evolution from republic to de-facto monarchy was long invoked as an argument against the establishment of republican forms at a wider scale than the city state. Influences can loom large. Perhaps this did delay something like republican government on a wider scale. Though set of course against the argument that not much urban republican social evolution had much in the way of prospects across much of Europe anyway!<br /> <br /> As much as I agree (with you and with Alucard, I think? feel free to say if I don't) that the Realm probably isn't much to do with the baseline level of authoritarian autocrats about in the Second Age, and that it does the Realm too much influence to suggest that this tradition of autocracy is their legacy in a world defined by amongst other phenomena er... a social history of about a thousand plus years of Solar god-kings. To degree there's a shared culture, it's not going to be &quot;And what *is* this 'autocracy' of which you speak?&quot; when the Realm gets going.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>, in lieu of a more substantive response on your post, to note it was full of interest. Again I feel like these things are more degrees of emphasis more than that I actually actively disagree with anything you've said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:24:04-07:00","id":1245983,"title":"","content":"Being good isn't the only qualification for being good at running a country. Administrative skill, charisma, the ability to resist bad influences, these are all important.<br /> <br /> But of course, being good is pretty important.<br /> <br /> I would assume, on average, Solars will be slightly better rulers than Dragonblood, because they are more skilled bureucrats, and better at socially influencing large groups of people.<br /> But that in no way proves any particular Solar is any better than any particular Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> And this is before we look at particular castes and note that the majority of Dawn castes are only marginally better at running a country than your average mortal, because they probably don't have any particular skill in Bureaucracy, Socialise, Integrity, etc. In fact, it's not an unreasonable argument that most Dawns might be worse at running a country than your average mortal; look at post-colonial Africa and S-E Asia where many heroic generals battled the evil Empires, won their nation's freedom, and then continued trying to use violence to solve their problems, because that was their skillset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T12:00:51-07:00","id":1246009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245983#post1245983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being good isn't the only qualification for being good at running a country. Administrative skill, charisma, the ability to resist bad influences, these are all important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but the ability of that charismatic administrator can just as easily be used to <i>churn out atrocities with machine-like efficiency.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T12:23:31-07:00","id":1246020,"title":"","content":"Hehe, all of this talk on various models of rulership had me thinking about a scenario in which something like democracy could exist.<br /> <br /> It hinges around the existence of Havesh.<br /> <br /> Nasty, grindy, <i>mercenary</i> Havesh.<br /> <br /> Havesh who, at the end of his story in the Caste book, is being forced to flee into the wilderness.<br /> <br /> Can you imagine Havesh ruling things? I can't. That's not even a question of him being technically capable of eventually developing the skills to do so; I just can't imagine him being bothered. Can't imagine him tolerating the hassle of it. Havesh doesn't want to run things, he just wants a life of ease and privilege. Preferably somebody <i>else</i>'s life of ease and privilege, but that can't last.<br /> <br /> He also has a certain sympathy for the underprivileged social stratum from which he originates. He outright despises the upper class of his homeland, and there's probably no love lost between him and the old Dragon Blooded hegemony. And as I recall, Havesh doesn't really like the idea of associating with other Solars, for a few reasons.<br /> <br /> So what is Havesh to do to get himself back from hiding in the wilderness to living the good life?<br /> <br /> I had this notion in which he spends the next several decades striking from the shadows to redistribute assets in his society a bit. Possibly something he came up with by himself, more likely something encouraged by some rebel or rabble rouser. He doesn't care for Varang's ancien regime, so he uses the subtle methods of the Night Caste to carefully dismantle it, and create the grounds for a new system. A more pluralistic system. A system in which those who were once lowest have some increased prospects.<br /> <br /> He doesn't do this out of rightenousness; he wants other people who will manage the tedium of running things, of keeping up the systems that ensure that there are nice things for him to buy as he retires to his gilded palace. People that will not infrequently have need for his services, and pay top dirham for them. Something that reconciles the better and worse parts of his nature. He resides within society, and is a major aspect in keeping it going, but he's not in charge, and is unconcerned with a lot of the specifics of what's going on.<br /> <br /> He's mercenary, but also somewhat pragmatic. It's probably hard to find something valuable enough to get him to actually betray his new Varang, not so much due to a sense of honour or national loyalty (although he might have a smidgeon of the latter) as a sense that whatever he would be paid to do amounts to shitting where he eats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T12:47:30-07:00","id":1246027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245983#post1245983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being good isn't the only qualification for being good at running a country. Administrative skill, charisma, the ability to resist bad influences, these are all important.<br /> <br /> But of course, being good is pretty important.<br /> <br /> I would assume, on average, Solars will be slightly better rulers than Dragonblood, because they are more skilled bureucrats, and better at socially influencing large groups of people.<br /> But that in no way proves any particular Solar is any better than any particular Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> And this is before we look at particular castes and note that the majority of Dawn castes are only marginally better at running a country than your average mortal, because they probably don't have any particular skill in Bureaucracy, Socialise, Integrity, etc. In fact, it's not an unreasonable argument that most Dawns might be worse at running a country than your average mortal; look at post-colonial Africa and S-E Asia where many heroic generals battled the evil Empires, won their nation's freedom, and then continued trying to use violence to solve their problems, because that was their skillset.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah, but solars get 5 favored abilities, and got no problem except 2 XP points more learning other charms. So, a dawn can learn how to be an efficeint bureaucrat just as fast as a DB can, he also has more powerful effects for that and he doesn't have to waste more power using them. On the other hand, a dragon blood of a certain element can't use presence or bureaucracy without more essence ( that's harder for them ) and without much more XP expenditure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T12:56:42-07:00","id":1246029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1245983#post1245983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being good isn't the only qualification for being good at running a country. Administrative skill, charisma, the ability to resist bad influences, these are all important.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's an important distinction to be made here between two different concepts, and using &quot;good&quot; for both of them is clouding the issue. You can be <i>competent</i> at running an organization/nation/empire/whatever - your orders are clear and easily understood, they make sense and use your resources to best advantage, you convince your followers to obey them happily, and so forth - without your goals in running things being <i>morally correct</i>. All the Exalted have the ability to achieve their goals with supernatural effectiveness. What <i>none</i> of them have is the supernatural ability to <i>choose the right goals</i>. Exalted has never put that into the hands of the characters, leaving it up to players and the ST to choose what's morally right. <br /> <br /> Now, I think it's true that, in the real world, there <i>is</i> a correlation between regimes that are morally worse and those run less effectively. If nothing else, empathy is a very useful tool for getting the best performance out of people, and morally corrupt regimes usually take actions that mean people involved have to suppress their own empathy to function. But this correlation is not 1-to-1 by any means, and some very evil nations or organizations have nonetheless accomplished a great deal in real history. And, Exalted is deliberately a game about exploring the nature of power and what people do with it, so I think ignoring the connection between morality and competence in the fiction is justified, to make for a more interesting set of choices for the characters.<br /> <br /> I can see someone in the setting, by the way, arguing that Dragonblooded are at least more likely to be moral rulers, since their powers are much more group-centric than other Exalts, and thus they're more likely to develop that sense of empathy that can prevent atrocities. I'm not making the argument myself, mind (I think the history of the setting pretty much suggests it doesn't hold water), but I can certainly see it being made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T13:19:56-07:00","id":1246036,"title":"","content":"Can't quote well on my phone.<br /> <br /> Ghosthead, yeah that was my basic point, that authoritarianism isn't necessarily based on the Realm. Though I'm not sure the legacy of Solar God-Kings is likely to be nearly as big an influence as the more diffuse Shogunate, purely due to time and propaganda. It's an interesting point though.<br /> One could argue that the Shogunate's power structure was a response to the Solar Deliberative anyway.<br /> <br /> Isator, I can definitely see that kind of thing.<br /> In my own game, Havesh led a Lunar-backed revolt by the Casteless, and became King of a new Casteless kingdom. Of course, he left all the boring admin to his No Moon assistant, who was much better at that kind of thing, while he enjoyed feasts and lovers, and murdered Realm spies and assassins. It was a good life until PCs murdered him for being suspicious while he was visiting his allies in Harborhead.<br /> <br /> Cruzwindt, it's a fair point about XP costs, but I can still say Water Aspects are better administrators than Dawns. They all favour bureaucracy. My point is... Dawns don't generally make good rulers.<br /> Saying this, the Dawn in my game has Bureaucracy 5, but he's a terrible ruler because his response to every problem is to invade it.<br /> <br /> We're close to putting our Essence 4 Night Caste on the throne in my other game (we've slowly got him up to possible heir, as the childless Pharoah's adopted brother) and... honestly, he'll be an awful ruler. He's naieve, blindly nationalistic, and his skills of stealing, sneaking, survival, awareness, endurance, athletics and wrestling are pretty irrelevant. Oh, also he threatens to chop off my head every few sessions. The mortal Pharoah, despite having done it for about a week, and having been raised as an aristocrat with a poor understanding of regular people's lives, is probably still a better ruler than the Night Caste. That's why you can't say Solars make better rulers. They're just too variable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T13:44:59-07:00","id":1246041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246036#post1246036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying this, the Dawn in my game has Bureaucracy 5, but he's a terrible ruler because his response to every problem is to invade it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say it like it's a bad thing !<br /> Lol, but seriously, as long as it's leader lives ,and it's mostly undefeated, a culture of only invading and plundering can survive, just look at the huns, they were all nomads who basically stole chinese culture and wares production and everyone's else through force. So a warrior without administration skills, can be an extremely efficient and good king capable of sustaining a vast and powerful empire .... now that his people is happy under his rule ... that's a complete different matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-14-2018, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T13:58:15-07:00","id":1246045,"title":"","content":"Well I think that whether the people are happy is a pretty important point (probably one of the most important points).<br /> But also the Huns... well, notice they're no longer here? They conquered for a while, and then lost to the locals because they'd expended too much strength fighting. Most tribal steppe invasions actually only last a few generations at most.<br /> As you said, as long as its leader lives, and it's mostly undefeated. But eventually, you get defeated and the leader dies.<br /> <br /> Constant invasion and plundering actually isn't what most Empires do. First they invade and plunder. But then they need a recurring tax base. This is why China was conquered multiple times by invading barbarians... who then Sinified and became just a new class of aristocrats ruling over peasants, because that's really how you sustain your power. Actually, conquering cultures tend to either settle down and create a base (which they may well use for more raids, but they will have that base as well), or they keep conquering, split and fight each other, and then get beaten themselves.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the issue with this Dawn is that he's got himself into a war with a Solar Sorceress, with the Realm ready to invade soon. If he thought more diplomatically, rather than &quot;the best way to defend places is to annex them&quot;, &quot;the best way to ensure the safety of my river's water source is to invade and conquer the mountains&quot; and &quot;the best way to feed my people is to conquer food-rich areas&quot;, then he could have easily taken a diplomatic option, allied with the Solar Sorceress who'd have sold him food from her magic farms, and they could conquer the Realm's nearby territories easily, making it very difficult for the Realm to project power here without local supplies.<br /> Whereas, under the previous ruler (a ghost with like War 1, and 4 mortal sub-kings), they got on well with all the local powers, and the Solar Sorceress even gave them dragons to use against enemy tribes, allowing them to defeat them easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-14-2018, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T14:28:48-07:00","id":1246057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246045#post1246045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the issue with this Dawn is that he's got himself into a war with a Solar Sorceress, with the Realm ready to invade soon. If he thought more diplomatically, rather than &quot;the best way to defend places is to annex them&quot;, &quot;the best way to ensure the safety of my river's water source is to invade and conquer the mountains&quot; and &quot;the best way to feed my people is to conquer food-rich areas&quot;, then he could have easily taken a diplomatic option, allied with the Solar Sorceress who'd have sold him food from her magic farms, and they could conquer the Realm's nearby territories easily, making it very difficult for the Realm to project power here without local supplies.<br /> Whereas, under the previous ruler (a ghost with like War 1, and 4 mortal sub-kings), they got on well with all the local powers, and the Solar Sorceress even gave them dragons to use against enemy tribes, allowing them to defeat them easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmm, and how dumb is the solar ? Is he completely ignorant of another forms of warfare besides attacking ? Or is he a genius mastermind of combat but nothing else ?<br /> Cuz if it's the second he could always use a false flag attacks to drive neighbor kingdoms unwillingly at his side, forcing them to be at their command or die at the hands of the ghost flag enemy that attacked them.<br /> Now if he is too honorable for that, or looking for an alternative to fighting a loosing war, then, I guess it's reincarnation for him.<br /> Another option would be burned land tactics, where he would let the enemy advance in position and acquire territory that's traps, contains venom or destroyed resources they cannot use to advance further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-14-2018, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T20:36:27-07:00","id":1246166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246027#post1246027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> yeah, but solars get 5 favored abilities, and got no problem except 2 XP points more learning other charms. So, a dawn can learn how to be an efficeint bureaucrat just as fast as a DB can, he also has more powerful effects for that and he doesn't have to waste more power using them. On the other hand, a dragon blood of a certain element can't use presence or bureaucracy without more essence ( that's harder for them ) and without much more XP expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thankfully these 2e assumptions are deaddeaddead in 3e. DBs as of WFHW get 5 aspect 5 favored, they only pay more for Evocations [which they use at a Celestial or Solar level] and spells, and the &quot;wrong element surcharge&quot; is gone, and the closest thing to it in 3e - the Aura keyword - is almost entirely missing from Bureaucracy with only one edge case [a bonus for Earth Aura making your organization incorruptible and absolutely loyal].<br /> <br /> Have I mentioned that 2e basically attempted character assassination on all non-Solar Exalts whether through incompetence or malice? 'Cause 2e basically attempted character assassination on all non-Solar Exalts whether through incompetence or malice.<br /> <br /> v: Ah, true, I discount alchemicals since they basically don't matter to Creation as a Whole, which means because they can't outshine Solars normally, they're allowed to shine instead of having muck gunked onto them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-15-2018, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T21:50:40-07:00","id":1246178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246166#post1246166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thankfully these 2e assumptions are deaddeaddead in 3e. DBs as of WFHW get 5 aspect 5 favored, they only pay more for Evocations [which they use at a Celestial or Solar level] and spells, and the &amp;quot;wrong element surcharge&amp;quot; is gone, and the closest thing to it in 3e - the Aura keyword - is almost entirely missing from Bureaucracy with only one edge case [a bonus for Earth Aura making your organization incorruptible and absolutely loyal].<br /> <br /> Have I mentioned that 2e basically attempted character assassination on all non-Solar Exalts whether through incompetence or malice? 'Cause 2e basically attempted character assassination on all non-Solar Exalts whether through incompetence or malice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, now, Alchies were portrayed pretty well, up to and including &quot;being the reason an alt-universe Realm doesn't go astray&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the Paragon tangent... while I'm all for deconstructing the mystique of empires and kings and such in Exalted, I do prefer Paragon as flip side where even if your absolute tyrant is a fairly benevolent guy with a genuine interest in his state's welfare... the end result is a 1984-esque state with a single point of failure currently stressed by a Solar disciple who can frankly do the Perfect's job better than he can. 'Cause having that be the result of someone who genuinely meant well as opposed to the Fantasy North Korea some folks go for says more to me than yet another petty king who grinds their subjects down for treasure, and (to link back to the topic) is a nice counterpoint and variation of the Realm itself; born from a woman who saved the world and spent the next couple of centuries building a horrible place in an effort to keep herself comfortable and the world saved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T05:34:30-07:00","id":1246274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246166#post1246166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thankfully these 2e assumptions are deaddeaddead in 3e. DBs as of WFHW get 5 aspect 5 favored, they only pay more for Evocations [which they use at a Celestial or Solar level] and spells, and the &quot;wrong element surcharge&quot; is gone, and the closest thing to it in 3e - the Aura keyword - is almost entirely missing from Bureaucracy with only one edge case [a bonus for Earth Aura making your organization incorruptible and absolutely loyal].<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But .... the 5 favored abilities for solars is also a first edition thing, together with the experience cost of charms. So is the essence surchange using charms that are not from your element....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246166#post1246166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> v: Ah, true, I discount alchemicals since they basically don't matter to Creation as a Whole, which means because they can't outshine Solars normally, they're allowed to shine instead of having muck gunked onto them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's blasphemy ! A game without the Locust Crusade it's not a game !. Lol, you are right, thought in retrospective I've always allowed to play Alchemicals as a point of start or later in the game with the assumption of the locust crusade already happened. Maybe I'm too permissive ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T05:40:45-07:00","id":1246277,"title":"","content":"Well wherever the surcharge first appeared, it's last was in 2e. DBs are a lot more flexible now, up to the level solars were in past editions. (Solars in 3e are even flexible-er)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T06:03:40-07:00","id":1246287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246274#post1246274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Maybe I'm too permissive ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do you, whatever works for your game. I just assume the reason alchemicals escaped the fate everyone else suffered - kneecapped to ensure Solars won the footrace - is because they weren't deemed a threat due to seal of eight divinities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T06:07:10-07:00","id":1246290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246045#post1246045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I think that whether the people are happy is a pretty important point (probably one of the most important points).</div> </div> </div> </div>But solars have social, presence, and mind control charms.<br /> <br /> Is that really reliable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T07:44:09-07:00","id":1246330,"title":"","content":"Well, if the people are miserable even when ruled by a social-fu Solar, then they must be a really bad ruler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T08:53:50-07:00","id":1246351,"title":"","content":"I love threads like this, because it's just post after post of apologia for empire. &quot;The Realm is not cartoonishly evil,&quot; no, it's not evil like a cartoon! It's evil in the way humans are evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T09:40:57-07:00","id":1246361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246351#post1246351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love threads like this, because it's just post after post of apologia for empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though it would be apologia for empire if there are people saying that its rationalizations are either accurate or justified, rather than noting their place amongst people that both have agendas and fallible perspectives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Realm is not cartoonishly evil,&quot; no, it's not evil like a cartoon! It's evil in the way humans are evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you still get variations there, although I'll admit that it can ultimately be a bit of a dog and pony show to try and define a scale and figure out where &quot;widespread execution and internment as a response to rebellion against a system of economic and political balance&quot; figures compared to, say, mass murder of people with glasses as an expression of general anti-intellectualism and a kind of reactionary primitivism.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T10:40:58-07:00","id":1246382,"title":"","content":"I think there's a diffference that's worth noting between &quot;the Realm brutally suppresses dissidents and is generally not great unless you absolutely toe the line and cause no trouble in which case it's still not great but at least it's not great in the sense that seeing your wealth siphoned off to foreign overlords is not great as opposed to being brutally executed is not great&quot;, IE realistically 'evil' if you want to use that term, vs &quot;the Realm has debauched parties where nobles loose summoned demons onto staff to rape and kill as said demons like because they're bored evil nobles, and absolutely noone sees anything wrong with or objectionable about this&quot; IE cartoonishly evil, malevolent for its' own sake.<br /> <br /> But sure, drawing that line means I'm apologizing for empire, you do you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T11:00:51-07:00","id":1246388,"title":"","content":"Plus, this thread is about the dragon blooded, not the realm.<br /> <br /> Outcastes are fine. They might well be fighting the big empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T11:10:26-07:00","id":1246391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246382#post1246382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a diffference that's worth noting between &quot;the Realm brutally suppresses dissidents and is generally not great unless you absolutely toe the line and cause no trouble in which case it's still not great but at least it's not great in the sense that seeing your wealth siphoned off to foreign overlords is not great as opposed to being brutally executed is not great&quot;, IE realistically 'evil' if you want to use that term, vs &quot;the Realm has debauched parties where nobles loose summoned demons onto staff to rape and kill as said demons like because they're bored evil nobles, and absolutely noone sees anything wrong with or objectionable about this&quot; IE cartoonishly evil, malevolent for its' own sake.<br /> <br /> But sure, drawing that line means I'm apologizing for empire, you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, I don't personally really care (it's always a little disconcerting I'll admit!), and I wasn't saying anything about you, in particular, but... &quot;well the Realm isn't all bad&quot; is an apologia for empire. It just is!<br /> <br /> The Realm <i>does </i>&quot;brutally suppress dissidents.&quot; It &quot;brutally pillages the wealth of the world and carts it all back to the Blessed Isle&quot;. It &quot;facilitates a global slave trade.&quot; It's an empire, i.e. a giant machine for elevating a privileged few to heights of luxury on the broken backs of the many. When I made the distinction about &quot;cartoonish evil&quot; this is exactly what I was talking about! No, the Dragon-Blooded of the Dynasty mostly do not do what you suggested, because they aren't cartoons. <br /> <br /> But they do, y'know, casually execute their slaves for minor infractions. They maintain harems of men and women who are legally considered to lack bodily autonomy. They tax entire countries into starvation in order to fund their war games (which will result in more starvation and more death). If evil exists at all, then that's evil! The Realm is evil and bad. <br /> <br /> That shouldn't impact your ability to play loyal members of the Dynasty, because people are complicated and we all live within oppressive systems, and i don't think the books need to come out and explicitly say &quot;empire is bad,&quot; but like, empire is bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T11:28:59-07:00","id":1246398,"title":"","content":"As apologia for empires go, &quot;Our empire is the biggest obstacle in the way of monsters from outside reality unraveling the bodies, minds, and souls of every last person&quot; is really an atypically good one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T11:36:54-07:00","id":1246400,"title":"","content":"Yes... but tbh, Lunars are probably the main obstacle on the way of Fae raiders, if only because they're closer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246388#post1246388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, this thread is about the dragon blooded, not the realm.<br /> <br /> Outcastes are fine. They might well be fighting the big empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as I said, you can't blame Lookshy for the Realm's invasions when they're literally fighting those invasions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T11:56:37-07:00","id":1246401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246398#post1246398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As apologia for empires go, &quot;Our empire is the biggest obstacle in the way of monsters from outside reality unraveling the bodies, minds, and souls of every last person&quot; is really an atypically good one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its a really really really common one though. I mean, not in the specific, but a good number of empires justify their use of force as being the light of civilization against barbarism. The Fae <i>in particular</i> are distinct, but to be honest their fairly far from the realm, and I doubt the Realm only invades areas to defend from the fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T12:49:08-07:00","id":1246411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246391#post1246391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I don't personally really care (it's always a little disconcerting I'll admit!), and I wasn't saying anything about you, in particular, but... &quot;well the Realm isn't all bad&quot; is an apologia for empire. It just is!</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people I've seen who've been saying that were comparing it to the factions who are going to destroy the world if nobody stops them.<br /> Such groups usually exist in fantasy and science fiction settings to offer ideological simplification so that hard men can make their hard decisions and there's clearly been points where Exalted has played that idea completely straight, which has made the stance on the Realm seem a little incoherent as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T13:58:13-07:00","id":1246426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246411#post1246411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people I've seen who've been saying that were comparing it to the factions who are going to destroy the world if nobody stops them.<br /> Such groups usually exist in fantasy and science fiction settings to offer ideological simplification so that hard men can make their hard decisions and there's clearly been points where Exalted has played that idea completely straight, which has made the stance on the Realm seem a little incoherent as a result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, and I've no interest in starting a fight (and indeed, I love the Realm as a setting and think it's very well-done primarily because it presents a realistic view of what empire <i>is</i> and <i>does</i> that is not immediately parsed as the Evil Empire Feat. Skull Motifs).<br /> <br /> That said, the justification of &quot;we protect you from the dead/the Fair Folk/the Lunar Anathema&quot; is mostly self-serving and not even particularly true. Like, what's the greatest danger looming over the people of the Blessed Isle? Is it the Mask of Winters? Is it a reborn Balorian Crusade? Nope! It's the civil war between the ruling powers, that will almost certainly decimate the countryside, all so they can promote somebody new to the Scarlet Throne (who will then proceed to re-conquer as much land as possible and resume brutal resource extraction). Look at any Cathak (or Peleps, or Tepet) satrapy-- what's the real problem? Is it ghosts, or is it the fact that legionnaires are shipping off your entire harvest to the Isle in preparation for said civil war?<br /> <br /> Obviously, that story isn't monolithic, and it's not necessarily the first thing that jumps out at you if you want to play a high fantasy save-the-whole-world Solar game. But it's there in black and white: that's what the Realm is doing. It isn't good, it isn't nice, and it absolutely is not pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","user":"Fitter Happier","date":". 08-15-2018, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T14:10:07-07:00","id":1246428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246400#post1246400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes... but tbh, Lunars are probably the main obstacle on the way of Fae raiders, if only because they're closer.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's about 400 Lunars <i>at maximum </i>at any given point in time. Going off the map, the border of Creation (to the extent that there is a border rather than a gradual shift, but I'm working with what I've got here) is about 56,000 miles in total. Despite those 400 Lunars generally being pushed to the edges of the world, they are demonstrably not all hanging out right on the edge of Creation - of all the established Lunar dominions, the <i>closest</i> to Creation's border is the Caul, which is 1800 miles away from the edge of the world. And that's a lot of those less-than-400 Lunars all staying in one place, actively fighting people who aren't the Fair Folk and therefore not doing anything to sail around searching for invaders from the Wyld trying to slip past their continent.<br /> <br /> The point here being that it would be <i>incredibly generous</i> to assume that there's one Lunar for every 560 miles of Creation's border, given how few there are in total and how many of the few we have are way deeper into the world than that. Moreover, those handful of Lunars who are way out on the edges of the world are going to be clumping together into circles at a significant frequency, so we'd very frequently be finding thousands of miles of Creation's border without a single Lunar anywhere to be seen. And in the really rare case that a bunch of fae raiders do have the tremendous misfortune of bumping into one of that scant handful of Lunars, there isn't even a particular reason to assume they'd fight. I'm not saying they wouldn't, or that it would be unreasonable of them to do battle, but if I'm fighting an endless guerilla war against the mightiest empire in Creation and I see an army of Wyld-born monsters marching towards said empire, I'm hardly going to risk my troops and my life in an attempt to stop them.<br /> <br /> So yes, sometimes raksha will try to invade Creation and be stopped by a Lunar, but it never made any sense for that to be marketed as a big Thing that Lunars do even in second edition where that was designed to be their Thing, and it makes absolutely no sense in third. The odds of your Wyld-spawned hordes being stopped by a heroic Lunar who just happened to be there when they invaded aren't meaningfully bigger than the odds of them being stopped by, like, a Liminal who was just wandering through on the way to hunt down a hungry ghost, and they're going to be much, much smaller than the odds that a band of spirits or particularly plucky mortals work together to defend their domain. And all of those things are less than the odds that the Realm, the ten thousand dragons who rule the world and the disciplined, well-equipped legions who serve them, will be the ones who end up stopping the march of the Fair Folk. Not because they're the good guys or because empires are awesome and happy places, but because they have the raw power required to do it, the numbers required to cover all that territory and the motivation to protect the lands they're currently plundering from other marauding parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 08-15-2018, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T14:39:36-07:00","id":1246432,"title":"","content":"You can certainly make a claim that lots of posts ITT are apologia for the Realm, if you choose to place the line there (they're not exactly late Kipling but I can't say it'd be incorrect). But what you couldn't do is consistently make the claim that they are and Grabowski's famous statement of (paraphrasing) &quot;...but the Realm also provides a basic check against anarchy in the Threshold, etc&quot; is not. I think he was right in his assessment that this was a more useful statement for him to provide than, for example, something along the lines of &quot;Empire is evil, the Realm is an empire, no positive utility can be imagined to flow from it and almost anything that is likely to replace it is will likely be an improvement&quot;. One of these contains ideas that we will go back to in order to discuss the Realm, one does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T15:11:27-07:00","id":1246443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246432#post1246432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can certainly make a claim that lots of posts ITT are apologia for the Realm, if you choose to place the line there (they're not exactly late Kipling but I can't say it'd be incorrect). But what you couldn't do is consistently make the claim that they are and Grabowski's famous statement of (paraphrasing) &quot;...but the Realm also provides a basic check against anarchy in the Threshold, etc&quot; is not. I think he was right in his assessment that this was a more useful statement for him to provide than, for example, something along the lines of &quot;Empire is evil, the Realm is an empire, no positive utility can be imagined to flow from it and almost anything that is likely to replace it is will likely be an improvement&quot;. One of these contains ideas that we will go back to in order to discuss the Realm, one does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do provide a basic check against anarchy in the Threshold... because anarchy makes resource extraction more difficult. They will also defend your farm when bandits ride in to carry off your children and crops... because <i>they</i> want your children and crops. <i>That's why the Realm is there at all. </i><br /> <br /> Like I said before, I agree that it is not useful for a published product to say, &quot;Empire is bad.&quot; But we, as readers, are more than capable of coming to that conclusion ourselves. The moral ambiguity doesn't come from &quot;is it OK for the Realm to brutally wring every last ounce of wealth from their satrapies if they, like, pave some roads (in order to extract wealth more efficiently)?&quot; That's not a difficult moral question. The moral ambiguity comes from &quot;and what do you intend to do about it?&quot; If you chase off the Imperial garrison, how do you intend to fend off bandits? If you remove the yoke of Imperial oppression, but then allow some local strongman to fill the power vacuum, does that make you a liberator? How does one rule well?<br /> <br /> At least, that's my opinion! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T16:25:52-07:00","id":1246465,"title":"","content":"\u201cGood, bad, I\u2019m the guy with the dragon sigh wand.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T16:37:28-07:00","id":1246466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246401#post1246401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a really really really common one though. I mean, not in the specific, but a good number of empires justify their use of force as being the light of civilization against barbarism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no, it's really not the same.<br /> <br /> Sure, there is a passing resemblance between &quot;Our empire protects civilization from being destroyed by barbarians&quot; and &quot;Our empire protects humanity itself from being utterly annihilated&quot;, but they are substantially different, starting with the fact that the barbarians are part of humanity. When barbarians knock over empires, at worst you get a dark age, and if you don't happen to be one of the peasants killed in the war itself, it's not clear how much you actually suffer because &quot;civilization&quot; fell. I mean, art and literature suffer, sure. Urban life declines. Ways of life change. But for the rural peasant farmer, how much does one actually notice the difference between the Romans and the Franks? Because only insofar as Roman oppression is better than life under the Franks is the Roman oppression justified to the peasant.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Balorian Crusade, if successful, would have meant the extinction of humanity and the end of all Creation.<br /> <br /> So when you're considering putting down a peasant revolt that really was a justified reaction against the excesses of a satrap, the balance-points differ. &quot;They're weakening the bulwark that allows art and literature and urban life to flourish, therefore we must put down the justified-in-itself revolt&quot; is morally a very different proposition than, &quot;They're weakening the bulwark that allows humanity, including themselves and their loved ones, to exist, therefore we must put down the justified-in-itself revolt.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, that doesn't make the Realm's crimes not crimes, and it is a perfectly fair question how much the Realm <i>actually</i> protects existence from extinction. But &quot;we protect humanity from nonexistence&quot; is a far, far better argument for empire than &quot;we protect civilization&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T17:39:05-07:00","id":1246484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246388#post1246388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, this thread is about the dragon blooded, not the realm.<br /> <br /> Outcastes are fine. They might well be fighting the big empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the Realm DBs might not be that bad, for the most part. The Realm is bad, but the truly insidious thing about great machines like an Empire or oppressive overseas labor exploitation is that you don't need a super large percentage of the people to be heartless dicks to make it work. There can be a lot of good people who really don't have any options, and who's contribution to trying to do the right thing amount to almost nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246443#post1246443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The moral ambiguity comes from &quot;and what do you intend to do about it?&quot; If you chase off the Imperial garrison, how do you intend to fend off bandits? If you remove the yoke of Imperial oppression, but then allow some local strongman to fill the power vacuum, does that make you a liberator? How does one rule well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue even then the issue isn't ambiguous at all. Chase off the imperial garrison, get the local people in a position where they can defend themselves from the enemies without and within, convince other neighboring nations to join a kind of NATO pact where they defend eachother, since no nation is strong enough to protect itself from a large focused assault. Then you probably introduce some kind of democracy to hold people to account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T00:49:33-07:00","id":1246561,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1201_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1201\" data-vbnamecard=\"1201\">Fitter Happier</a>, I don't think you're wrong, though as we're on the whys I think you may be underestimating the Realm as empire of faith and ideology and as defence. <br /> <br /> Even if the Realm stood in a region to gain no profit, even should the entire Threshold not be profitable, my guess is they'd go out and conquer it because the Immaculate Philosophy presents the Perfected Hierarchy, with the Dragon blooded in command, as the appropriate spiritual condition of the world. If there were nothing to extract, they'd grumble and spend the revenues from their isle holdings to no material profit to uphold their belief.<br /> <br /> (This is not a &quot;good&quot; motivation really, its just not purely material. At the same time, its the ideology that does frame that quote by GCG about how (paraphrasing) Dynasts can be enormously brutal rulers who then go out and sacrifice themselves in battle for some uneconomically unimportant village, and that they often genuinely do aspire to being the enlightened samurai supermen that the Immaculate Philosophy says they are.)<br /> <br /> There's also the defense aspect; even if the Threshold were bleeding money from isle holdings, the Realm would run its empire because they are scared of not having a buffer of states between them and mortal kingdoms, the Lunar Exalted, dead and fae, and other powers (and for good reason).<br /> <br /> (Again not really &quot;good&quot; and self interest of a sort, but not material in the sense of motivated only by wealth).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>, that could work, though &quot;nation building&quot; is hard and full of unintended consequence, as has been discovered, and I think most potential nations of Creation would be harder, and compromise with the powers about would change how that works out. But I guess would strike me as something more likely for powerful earth people transported to Creation (A Connecticut Yankee stuff) not something that people in the setting would immediately leap to, or evolve through experience, and less so a Solar Exalted with visions of the First Age in his head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T05:17:53-07:00","id":1246606,"title":"","content":"Looking back at one of Dan Olson's videos about Man of Steel, I feel a need to remind myself that there's a certain necessary metatextual analysis of the apocalyptic scenario that the Realm was given in the first place, and how much the underlying premise of that might constitute an apologia for imperialism. It's like Lioness referenced a few posts back; the point that a good deal of fantasy and science fiction revolves around irreconcilably hostile enemies as a means of letting certain kinds of power fantasies play out without criticism.<br /> <br /> Or hell, even in-character, there might be somebody who has a basis for making a certain Mad Max Fury Road argument to the effect of &quot;no, our broken down world does not in fact necessitate or benefit from this kind of militaristic authoritarian power structure, because that (or at least the premises and world view underlying it) is what got us into this mess in the first place&quot;.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't exactly call the Scarlet Empress evil, but for a character profile I'd at least go with the idea that her critical examination of the failure points of the Shogunate would have been rather limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T19:00:19-07:00","id":1246840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246466#post1246466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, it's really not the same.<br /> <br /> Sure, there is a passing resemblance between &quot;Our empire protects civilization from being destroyed by barbarians&quot; and &quot;Our empire protects humanity itself from being utterly annihilated&quot;, but they are substantially different, starting with the fact that the barbarians are part of humanity. When barbarians knock over empires, at worst you get a dark age, and if you don't happen to be one of the peasants killed in the war itself, it's not clear how much you actually suffer because &quot;civilization&quot; fell. I mean, art and literature suffer, sure. Urban life declines. Ways of life change. But for the rural peasant farmer, how much does one actually notice the difference between the Romans and the Franks? Because only insofar as Roman oppression is better than life under the Franks is the Roman oppression justified to the peasant.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Balorian Crusade, if successful, would have meant the extinction of humanity and the end of all Creation.<br /> <br /> So when you're considering putting down a peasant revolt that really was a justified reaction against the excesses of a satrap, the balance-points differ. &quot;They're weakening the bulwark that allows art and literature and urban life to flourish, therefore we must put down the justified-in-itself revolt&quot; is morally a very different proposition than, &quot;They're weakening the bulwark that allows humanity, including themselves and their loved ones, to exist, therefore we must put down the justified-in-itself revolt.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, that doesn't make the Realm's crimes not crimes, and it is a perfectly fair question how much the Realm <i>actually</i> protects existence from extinction. But &quot;we protect humanity from nonexistence&quot; is a far, far better argument for empire than &quot;we protect civilization&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually worth noting, that in 3e at least, there probably isn't probably ever going to be, nor ever was going to be, another Balorian Crusade. It was a one-off event that likely Creation might just not see again. A big reason 3e is moving away from existential, world-ending plots like a second Baloriain Crusade is actually so that things like this well, do have ambiguity. The Realm ciould say they are the balwark agains the Fair Folk coming back, but to be fair, they never were going to come until Balor and they never will come again in the lifetime of an emprie.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Basically, giving the empire &quot;No, really we're the necessary evil&quot; is probably not good if you want to not seem to be indulging in imperial apoligia I htink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T00:56:55-07:00","id":1246907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246466#post1246466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, the Balorian Crusade, if successful, would have meant the extinction of humanity and the end of all Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Balorian Crusade was ended by the Realm Defense Grid. Nothing any Exalted outside the Empress and her companions did had anything to do with it; as far as we know, it would have gone down exactly the same way if she had been the only Dragon-Blood in existence.<br /> <br /> But much more importantly, the Realm Defense Grid continued to protect against Fair Folk incursions regardless of what else the Empress did. The argument that she provided some additional protection by immediately turning around and aiming it at the remnants of the Shogunate is flatly a lie (if anything, she left the Dragon-Blooded <i>weaker</i> in the immediate aftermath of that conflict.)<br /> <br /> It's not like you can really argue that the Fair Folk Invasion was a failure of the Shogunate, even. It's not at all clear that there's anything they could have done against the one-two punch of the Great Contagion and the Fair Folk invasion. And if the Realm Defense Grid broke down at any point in the Realm's history, followed by another Contagion + Fair Folk invasion, the Realm would have collapsed just as fast as the Shogunate did (in fact, probably faster.) Brutally murdering a bunch of Dragon-Blooded in order to form a new political order with her at the head didn't really make Creation any safer or stronger. All it accomplished was ensuring that its political order had a single point of failure and could easily fail catastrophically.<br /> <br /> The Empress <i>could</i> have chosen to maintain the Realm Defense Grid as a reclusive monk who used it only against dangers to Creation, for instance, refusing to get involved in any political struggles between nations. She could have recruited and trained a small force to back this up. She could even, you know, have taught someone else to use it, which would be pretty important if, say, she were to unexpectedly die or disappear or something. She did none of these things.<br /> <br /> (The last one in particular is probably her most glaring failure. But it's illustrative in that it shows how she was either primarily concerned with maintaining and extending her own power; or completely consumed with paranoia to the point where she didn't feel that <i>anyone</i> but her could be trusted to safeguard Creation's future.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 08-17-2018, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T02:32:56-07:00","id":1246926,"title":"","content":"Note that the reference to Greyfalls in What Fire Has Wrought suggests that the Realm Defence Grid is somewhat less centralised now, and at least some of the imperialism is based on taking control of its distributed components so that they can be secured and maintained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T03:13:54-07:00","id":1246940,"title":"","content":"I do wonder if, in a world where we had to rewrite Exalted's base setting assumptions, I wouldn't do away with the RDG in favour of the Empress as more of a directly Shi Huang Di esque figure, putting together the strongest state among feuding Dragonblooded through radical reforms, harnessing the power of faith in the new Immaculate Philosophy as her state ideology and securing the backing of the Bronze Faction, then unifying the warring states. And make all this still very morally questionable as a long term path for the world and at the time.<br /> <br /> Maybe even do away with the Balorian Crusade and Great Contagion as singular things, rather than the slow toll of disorder among the Dragonblooded and inadequacy to deal with smaller incursions and the gradual failure of First Age infrastructure in the absence of Solar geniuses. Plus attribute more loss since the First Age to Usurpation era destruction.<br /> <br /> There are just so many questions that the apocalypse elements introduce - &quot;How is this actually compatible with Sidereal astrology and the Great Prophecy?&quot; being a recent one we've gone over and over - and the means that they are resolved are treated somewhat as an afterthought to the actual politics and central concerns of the setting - to exaggerate:&quot;Oh hai guys, btw, the numberless Fair Folk could almost destroy the world, the Deathlords have super-bio weapons, the Sidereals could do nothing to plan for or prevent any of this, but it's all good because the Empress has a cache of nukes (which only very occasionally enter as a deus ex machina) and we're just not gonna talk about this too much in the actual business of the setting&quot;. The tools the Empress is described as using to build her Realm are not that integral to the means she used to gain it...<br /> <br /> Either that or walk into these elements and yeah, work to more actively make maintaining a continued bulwark keeping the Fae divided, maintaining magical defenses of the Realm, managing plagues of magical origin, using magical weapons to maintain and hold power, worrying about the emergence of apocalyptic forces; all of this much more of a element of pre-occupation to the status quo powers of the setting, and something which they *do*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T03:34:07-07:00","id":1246945,"title":"","content":"I really don't see how the prophecy is harmed. &quot;But Creation was almost destroyed, twice!!!!!&quot;<br /> And yet against all odds it survives.<br /> Almost as if that was its fate.<br /> As if it was destined to survive, lessened, but intact.<br /> Like a subtle hand guided heroes through chance and circumstance to where they needed to be in Creation's darkest hour to stand against the tide of darkness and protect Creation.<br /> <br /> Almost as if it were preordained that Creation would survive, lessened but alive, to see the Dawn of another age.<br /> <br /> But that wasn't what the prophecy said, so it must be an invalid prophecy -- wait you mean that's exactly what the prophecy said to the letter? Huh, funny.<br /> <br /> Edit: funny note. Almost no Sidereal charms even in 2e, the anti Sidereal edition, actually fail against creatures outside of fate unless they are mentally affecting them. Prior Warning and Expected Pain for example by raw work just fine against an infernal or third circle attacking you, letting you see it coming<br /> <br /> Edit 2: an important thing to remember about Sidereal prophecy and destiny is that they aren't just pretty words. Check out Of Things Desired and Feared, I believe. <br /> &quot;I want this to happen.'<br /> &quot;The price is this.&quot;<br /> &quot;I accept the price&quot;<br /> &quot;Then so shall it be.&quot;<br /> The vision of Bronze didn't end with the last solar dying. It ends around the time Kejak dies; &quot;how ironic that one not my chosen should see the end of not one age but two.&quot;, Says Saturn.<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-17-2018, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T03:46:13-07:00","id":1246948,"title":"","content":"I suppose you can argue it in those terms.<br /> <br /> It's not so much in any sense the terms the original developer had at all in mind, though - <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/DBsVsSolars:\" target=\"_blank\">http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Sp...i/DBsVsSolars:</a> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Then Dragon-Blooded daimyo fought Dragon-Blooded daimyo for centuries, squandering their legacy of power, until the Great Contagion <b>(guess that astrology wasn't infallible after all, huh?) </b>killed 90% of the population, opened the gate to the armies of the Fair Folk, and wiped away the decaying remains of the First Age almost completely.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> But then the setting is a thing under further, different hands and Death of the Author and all that.<br /> <br /> Removing the Great Contagion would largely cut through those arguments, than that it's not arguable I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T03:48:30-07:00","id":1246949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246940#post1246940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder if, in a world where we had to rewrite Exalted's base setting assumptions, I wouldn't do away with the RDG in favour of the Empress as more of a directly Shi Huang Di esque figure, putting together the strongest state among feuding Dragonblooded through radical reforms, harnessing the power of faith in the new Immaculate Philosophy as her state ideology and securing the backing of the Bronze Faction, then unifying the warring states. And make all this still very morally questionable as a long term path for the world and at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds interesting. I would like to explore it.<br /> <br /> So what are we thinking; the Scarlet Empress as somebody who just happened to attain success through a combination of hard work, good ideas and a bit of luck that managed to outdo a number of rivals, or somebody who seized an opportunity that arose from a crisis point that left a lot of the old assumptions vulnerable, but not so extreme as &quot;most of the world ended&quot;?<br /> <br /> I have an image right now of the endemic warfare managing to exhaust resources to a point that the Dragon Blooded were suddenly very vulnerable to the Lunar Exalted, and the success of the Empress was in being able to martial and consolidate a significant number of them into a system to more efficiently concentrate limited resources that managed to prevent the Lunars from making a major advance. However, I'm also wondering if that might not just be the Great Contagion with different set dressing... no, not necessarily. Not if it didn't have a principle that the victory of the Other would entail the end of <i>everything</i>, rather than just the end of Dragon Blooded organised into a collectivized system reigning supreme.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'm interested in seeing where this might go.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T04:35:29-07:00","id":1246959,"title":"","content":"Let me be the first to say then, fuck grabowski in the eye. XP that's like saying the secret service failed in their job because 9/11. Their job is the president. Other intelligence agencies are responsible for that sort of thing. Or that a doctor who amputated a leg too far gone to gangrene failed his Hippocratic oath; I saved the patient's life, his leg wasn't part of the deal. Better he can argue whether life with one leg is worth living because he's alive than be dead. One of these can be fixed.<br /> If he seriously argues that Creation being alive but lessened disproves the prophecy which in very specific terms says Creation would survive alive but lessened (without any indication about how lessened) he should take a long walk off a short pier.<br /> The purpose of prophecy isn't to be wrong so we can laugh about dumb prophets, it's....a genie, where you get what you asked for and ask yourself &quot;was it worth it?&quot;<br /> That's the real gold versus bronze question. Not who was right but if the cost was justifiable<br /> 2e was constant and unending with the &quot;lol the seers didn't see something coming isn't it ironic it's like rain on your wedding day&quot; and basically missed the memo that if a group has an ostensibly functional power but you only ever being that power front and center when it doesn't work, well, you get to the forum fandom attitude as it now where the idea that the prophecy might have actually had any accuracy to it is somehow transgressive, why would the see-nothing seers have seen something this one time?<br /> <br /> V: EXACTLY.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-17-2018, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T04:43:20-07:00","id":1246961,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can see the sids during the shogunate being all &quot;oh, this isn't too bad. Yeah, I can live with this amount of lessened&quot;<br /> <br /> And then the contagion hit and they were all<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Shit.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T05:00:31-07:00","id":1246964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246959#post1246959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me be the first to say then, fuck grabowski in the eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Damn, I keep being dissatisfied with sardonic responses.<br /> <br /> I feel as though escalation such as this is not very conductive to good conversation. Even if it's being employed ironically, it's unpleasant enough to put me off of engaging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-17-2018, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T05:13:04-07:00","id":1246968,"title":"","content":"That's fine. I'm tired of the person who apparently started the &quot;the Sids can't be shown to be right about anything&quot; trend. His authority no matter how fundamental he was to 1e design is rendered worthless by his decision to start saying &quot;oh but it turns out it was a false dilemma all along because their powers don't actually work roflmao&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you're going to sabotage a player exalt type then don't be a fucking coward, be forthright about it. Tell front and goddamned center in Exalted the Sidereals, &quot;Sidereals will always be chumped by the universe taking a big stinking crap on them, their powers never work when they need to, and the fiction will never let them be awesome. Things you should know before you become a fan of them for prophecy abilities that don't work and fate bending abilities that won't be allowed to matter&quot;.<br /> Yeah it'll probably sell a lot fewer copies but being a prick presenting these cool character concepts and giggling to yourself about how much you're going to render them looking incompetent will only earn you unending ire &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-17-2018, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T05:54:53-07:00","id":1246983,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>, I hadn't really thought that deeply into the actual circumstances of how the Empress would rise to power under that scenario; it does feel right for her to both be an unusual and talented outsider and her rise precipitated by a crisis point (for which it may be a good idea to marshal in the Lunar Exalted, as if nothing else, this builds the Wyld Hunt and the Realm's struggle against the Lunar Exalted into the narrative and institutions of the Realm in a fundamental way, as well as represent a point for divergence in the fundamental way the Lunars approach the Dragonblooded).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"756\" data-vbnamecard=\"756\">Meianno Yuurei</a>, I feel a bit sorry for bringing that up quote in a way and if it came across as a bit of a &quot;gotcha&quot;. Other than repeating that perhaps he got it wrong in that quote and that things have moved (and maybe it is more solid for setting if the invasion of the Fair Folk and Great Contagion should be considered as part of the outcome of the vision of Bronze), I would just say it does seem really hard to manage and talk about prediction powers like the Sidereals so that they aren't either the ur-power (&quot;I know everything so I can secretly control everything&quot;) or ur-powerlessness for all (&quot;My predictions are so good that even I can't change anything!&quot;), and some of the nuances of things can fall away in old posts where people are just quoting hot in a discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T06:15:35-07:00","id":1246988,"title":"","content":"Lemme give a parallel.<br /> <br /> Aquaman is actually really damn strong. But you wouldn't know that if you only watched scenes where he wasn't strong enough and we needed Superman strength. You'd think his strength was a joke.<br /> <br /> 2e never showed anything to build up Sidereal heat. It tries to do the &quot;they're successful because of the thousands apocalypses you haven't heard of because they prevented them&quot; but that doesn't work. And then they cut it down by punctuating too many things with &quot;teehee they didn't see it isn't it ironic, like a traffic jam when you're already late&quot;. Contagion, crusade, prison, and most recent, Lotus massacre. Possibly others.<br /> <br /> So their one notable successful act, debatably, was the prophecy. The book presents it as accurate - costly, fraught with sacrifice and peril, but accurate; 100% chance of less than 100% casualties vs unknown percentage chance of absolute casualties, everything dead.<br /> <br /> And then this jackanape says &quot;nah brah it wasn't accurate, it was only sheer luck Firecrotch busted into the imperial manse and saved everyone from their Yet Another Fuck Up&quot;...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-17-2018, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T09:29:54-07:00","id":1247047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246907#post1246907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... (The last one in particular is probably her most glaring failure. But it's illustrative in that it shows how she was either primarily concerned with maintaining and extending her own power; or completely consumed with paranoia to the point where she didn't feel that <i>anyone</i> but her could be trusted to safeguard Creation's future.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In a way, i'ts a standard habit of a lot of dictators and conquerers in times.<br /> <br /> &quot;What happens when you die?&quot;<br /> &quot;It's not my problem anymore then is it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 08-17-2018, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T09:37:56-07:00","id":1247048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246959#post1246959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me be the first to say then, fuck grabowski in the eye.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Alternatively we could not say that.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T09:40:04-07:00","id":1247049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246988#post1246988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lemme give a parallel.<br /> <br /> Aquaman is actually really damn strong. But you wouldn't know that if you only watched scenes where he wasn't strong enough and we needed Superman strength. You'd think his strength was a joke.<br /> <br /> 2e never showed anything to build up Sidereal heat. It tries to do the &amp;quot;they're successful because of the thousands apocalypses you haven't heard of because they prevented them&amp;quot; but that doesn't work. And then they cut it down by punctuating too many things with &amp;quot;teehee they didn't see it isn't it ironic, like a traffic jam when you're already late&amp;quot;. Contagion, crusade, prison, and most recent, Lotus massacre. Possibly others.<br /> <br /> So their one notable successful act, debatably, was the prophecy. The book presents it as accurate - costly, fraught with sacrifice and peril, but accurate; 100% chance of less than 100% casualties vs unknown percentage chance of absolute casualties, everything dead.<br /> <br /> And then this jackanape says &amp;quot;nah brah it wasn't accurate, it was only sheer luck Firecrotch busted into the imperial manse and saved everyone from their Yet Another Fuck Up&amp;quot;...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m hoping the Sidereal book fixes a lot of this, like the DB book did. Before WFHW the second edition successful Wild Hunts that we saw on screen were killing a young eclipse, killing a VERY young eclipse, and a pretty unspecified Tepet Arada backstory where he defeated another eclipse in combat. <br /> <br /> Then 3e core comes out and the DB fiction is of a magistrate, one of the most powerful and intelligent agents of the empress, investigating, falling into a trap, running, getting caught, fighting, getting beaten, and then finally ends with the implication that she\u2019s going to be the lieutenant of this big sexy man who\u2019s pledged to tear down her homeland. It\u2019s actually well written, and kudos for making a cool dawn who\u2019s very social and for making an older woman somebody who\u2019s not a totally asexual creature, but come on! Where in that story is the idea that either Terrestrials are worthy foes or heroes in their own right?<br /> <br /> What we need is a Sidereal book where you\u2019ve got star chosen being competent, without totally crippling corruption, and 100% at least one scene where a circle of other exalted all gearing up for some specific great battle that they end up never having to fight because before they even see the enemy the sidereals have stopped the war.<br /> <br /> Oh and another fiction like the 2e intro to the sidereal book where they were all working together and making friendly jabs at each others political positions and stuff. That was among a very very few fictions/comics where I thought \u201cThis! This is what the game looks like when you\u2019re playing it.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T10:28:37-07:00","id":1247066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246945#post1246945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't see how the prophecy is harmed. &quot;But Creation was almost destroyed, twice!!!!!&quot;<br /> And yet against all odds it survives.<br /> Almost as if that was its fate..</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the Fair Folk and the Underworld (which was the origin of the Great Contagion) are outside of fate's purview. Creation survived that because of luck or, if you prefer, because that's just the way things happened, like in the real world. But it wasn't preserved by any sort of fate. That was literally the entire reason that &quot;outside of fate&quot; was created as a category. And there's important reasons it was set up that way...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's fine. I'm tired of the person who apparently started the &quot;the Sids can't be shown to be right about anything&quot; trend. </div> </div> </div>Several things to keep in mind:<br /> <br /> 1. The Sidereals don't have to be right all the time in order to be effective at what they're supposed to do. They just have to be right often enough for their choices to make sense and for their powers to be effective. Nobody <i>else</i>, note, gets to be right all the time - either in or outside the setting. The game absolutely supports the reading that the Primordial War was a mistake, that the way the Solars structured the First Age was a mistake, that the Shogunate and the Realm were mistakes, that everything the Lunars have done was a mistake. It doesn't <i>force</i> these, and I think the intended reading is more that they were imperfect and can be improved on, but they're clearly flawed. The Great Prophecy and the Usurpation are no different. They can be defensible, and reasonable, and something that makes sense in the backstory and supports the effectiveness of Sidereal powers, while also leaving open the reading that they were mistakes or that some element of them was fundamentally wrong. Nobody would expect Solar swordsmanship or management to be flawless, in the sense of never failing; it's silly to expect Sidereal prophecy to be flawless. It just has to be good enough for their actions to make sense.<br /> <br /> 2. Part of the reason for this is because all splats are optional, and players are meant to be free to choose where they focus the game. The game does not <i>require</i> that the world be saved by Solars. It doesn't require that whatever solution players come up with resemble the Realm. Similarly, the game does not require that you follow Fate or conform to Sidereal prophecy. &quot;Screw destiny&quot; always has to be available as an option, which means &quot;the Great Prophecy was flatly wrong&quot; or &quot;the Sidereals flatly misread it&quot; have to be available as options. They're not appropriate for all games, but they have to be there, and the game has always been careful to leave them there. And I disagree with the assertion that this would negate the effectiveness or importance of Sidereals (just like &quot;you can save the world without Solars&quot; doesn't negate the importance of Solars) - going for that outcome is obviously not what you'd do if you wanted to make the Sidereal story front-and-center, but narratively it's completely defensible as long as the decisions Sidereals made made sense at the time; even faced with <i>incontrovertible</i> evidence that the Sidereal reading of the Great Prophecy was flatly, indisputably, completely wrong, Kejak can still credibly say &quot;we knew that was a possibility, but the risk was too great.&quot; This is how people make hard decisions like that in the real world. More generally, the Sidereal theme is not and has never been about being <i>perfect</i> - about never getting it wrong. It's about having a layer of knowledge past what other people do, and making difficult decisions based on that knowledge. The fact that they sometimes get it wrong is an essential part of that story in the same way that eg. the fact that even the greatest Solar swordsman sometimes loses a fight and dies is a vital part of his story.<br /> <br /> 3. It's not true that the one notable successful Sidereal act was the prophecy. Their most important historical act was the <i>decision</i> to enact the Usurpation. The game cannot and will not ever canonically tell you if this was the right decision or not (although individual games may of course weigh in on one side or the other), but it's the reality of that decision and its aftermath that defines the Sidereals, not &quot;our prophecy is always right.&quot; They became the secret masters of the universe by having faith in their abilities and the willingness to seize power through violence in order to save the world and find the best path forwards. Whether they made the <i>right</i> choice or not is mostly immaterial at this point (as a modern-day young Sidereal, you didn't participate in that decision and can reasonably weigh in on either side.) The much more important thing is what that decision says about the Sidereals and the overarching themes it sets for them into the present day, ie. as a Sidereal, you are the person sitting on a secret throne in Heaven making vital decisions for everyone else.<br /> <br /> 4. I sort of hinted at this above, but really... everyone in Exalted has fucked up. The game's past is not intended to be a manual for how to do things in the future. The Exalted and the gods wage war against their enemies at the dawn of time with glorious excess (and got cursed as a result); the First Age was a time of glorious madness when the Solars failed to rein in their own impulses or recognize what they were doing wrong; the Shogunate was an era of noble decline; the Realm was an exercise in glorious brutality, and the Lunars are... the Lunars, let's not even go there. Compared to these the Sidereals have largely come closest to constant success - they've mostly gotten what they wanted at each point in the timeline. But like everyone else, their past successes are qualified, and some of that qualification is in questions related to their hubris and whether they've really been making the right choices.<br /> <br /> 5. If you make <i>everything</i> flawlessly governed by Fate, and just happening according to Fate, what happens to the heroic spirit? What does it say about the Empress (who is, after all, the greatest Dragon-Blooded hero), if her achievement wasn't entirely her own but was the fulfillment of some ancient Sidereal prophecy? Of course, this isn't an easy thing to answer - most stories that deal with fate have to grapple with what it means for free will, the heroic spirit and so on. But it's a complicated question, and the game wouldn't be served by saying &quot;the Empress was just a tool of Fate&quot; or whatever. The idea that the Empress genuinely saved Creation - that, if she had not done what she did, if she'd been a bit less heroic, everything might have died - is pretty important to her story and to the backstory of the Realm; narratively, that has at least as much heft as the Great Prophecy. She needs to have as much claim to saving Creation as Kejak Chejop. My point is that, for many players, &quot;everything you've done has been ACCORDING TO THE PROPHECY&quot; is going to be unfun and unsatisfying; and since the game does not revolve solely around Sidereals, it needs to provide support for such players, giving them escape hatches that they can use to thumb their nose at Fate.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's a tricky balancing act, because you don't want to risk damaging the grandeur or significance of Fate in games that do care about it (a problem that previous editions have sometimes grappled with.) But my point is, there are plenty of reasons to avoid making Sidereal readings of Fate flawless; and the Sidereal game doesn't <i>depend</i> on it being flawless, just on it being good enough that their actions are defensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T10:42:51-07:00","id":1247075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247049#post1247049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then 3e core comes out and the DB fiction is of a magistrate, one of the most powerful and intelligent agents of the empress, investigating, falling into a trap, running, getting caught, fighting, getting beaten, and then finally ends with the implication that she\u2019s going to be the lieutenant of this big sexy man who\u2019s pledged to tear down her homeland. It\u2019s actually well written, and kudos for making a cool dawn who\u2019s very social and for making an older woman somebody who\u2019s not a totally asexual creature, but come on! Where in that story is the idea that either Terrestrials are worthy foes or heroes in their own right?<br /> <br /> What we need is a Sidereal book where you\u2019ve got star chosen being competent, without totally crippling corruption, and 100% at least one scene where a circle of other exalted all gearing up for some specific great battle that they end up never having to fight because before they even see the enemy the sidereals have stopped the war.<br /> <br /> Oh and another fiction like the 2e intro to the sidereal book where they were all working together and making friendly jabs at each others political positions and stuff. That was among a very very few fictions/comics where I thought \u201cThis! This is what the game looks like when you\u2019re playing it.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that 3e is mostly being written with mixed games in mind. I suspect there's a very specific effort to avoid chapter fiction that plays up one splat at the cost of another, or which downplays other splats or could likewise encourage bad blood between players.<br /> <br /> Something like &quot;and then the Sidereal revealed a hidden truth that made all the contributions and preparation of other types of Exalted meaningless!&quot; isn't really something you want in the chapter fiction. It's not something you want to encourage players to aim for in a mixed game, and isn't really how you want players to get their first introduction for how Sidereals interact with the rest of the setting. For Sidereal players, either they'll fail and get frustrated, or they'll succeed and piss off everyone else; and if I'm the ST or a player of another splat skimming that book to decide if I want to let someone play a Sidereal, reading a chapter like that is going to make me say &quot;hell no, I don't want something like that in my game!&quot;<br /> <br /> This has been a particular problem for Sidereals in the past, since many players are put off by the &quot;we're the true secret masters!&quot; theme and the &quot;hidden underlying truth&quot; thematic. Some of that is unavoidable - you see similar resistance to the core theme of Solars, after all core splat or no, and you can't tone it down if it's what they are and what makes them fun to play - but it's a reason to try and use the chapter fiction to smooth over this and show ways that Sidereals can be worked into games. &quot;Here's a Sidereal being better than everyone!&quot; isn't a good way to accomplish that. (Just like, say, you don't want the intro Solar fiction to portray Gaston, because you'd be playing up the problems people already have with them. Note that the Solar intro fiction is low-key and has them screwing up in several ways; the Solar survives but partially because of outside intervention, and is pretty clearly endangered by the Wyld Hunt.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T12:14:01-07:00","id":1247113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1246926#post1246926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that the reference to Greyfalls in What Fire Has Wrought suggests that the Realm Defence Grid is somewhat less centralised now, and at least some of the imperialism is based on taking control of its distributed components so that they can be secured and maintained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangent: I had an idea for an Exalted board game/videogame/plot hook where taking control of the Sword of Creation in a specific region was the central macguffin of the campaign.<br /> <br /> I find it interesting that we might be seeing more explicit support for that campaign idea in the game line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T12:18:48-07:00","id":1247116,"title":"","content":"I think that it's all right for Sidereal prophecy to be fallible, but I think that, even with the Great Curse, there's an issue with the idea that they're widely unaware of a blindspot regarding things like the Underworld or Wyld.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I feel as though prophecies around the Usurpation should have been fairly focused on the subject of the Solars, rather than making promises about the distant future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T12:23:56-07:00","id":1247119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247116#post1247116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it's all right for Sidereal prophecy to be fallible, but I think that, even with the Great Curse, there's an issue with the idea that they're widely unaware of a blindspot regarding things like the Underworld or Wyld.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I feel as though prophecies around the Usurpation should have been fairly focused on the subject of the Solars, rather than making promises about the distant future.</div> </div> </div> </div>So like:<br /> <br /> Gold - there's a 60% chance of the solars continuing being huge assholes, a 35% chance of them destroying the entire world, killing everyone, and a 5% chance of everything getting so much better<br /> Bronze- There's a 100% chance that the solars won't destroy the world. The DBs will take over and it won't be as good, but things will keep running<br /> <br /> Chejop - &quot;Let's go with the Solars not murdering everyone and destroying everything, yeah?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T12:41:09-07:00","id":1247122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247075#post1247075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that 3e is mostly being written with mixed games in mind. I suspect there's a very specific effort to avoid chapter fiction that plays up one splat at the cost of another, or which downplays other splats or could likewise encourage bad blood between players.<br /> <br /> Something like &quot;and then the Sidereal revealed a hidden truth that made all the contributions and preparation of other types of Exalted meaningless!&quot; isn't really something you want in the chapter fiction. It's not something you want to encourage players to aim for in a mixed game, and isn't really how you want players to get their first introduction for how Sidereals interact with the rest of the setting. For Sidereal players, either they'll fail and get frustrated, or they'll succeed and piss off everyone else; and if I'm the ST or a player of another splat skimming that book to decide if I want to let someone play a Sidereal, reading a chapter like that is going to make me say &quot;hell no, I don't want something like that in my game!&quot;<br /> <br /> This has been a particular problem for Sidereals in the past, since many players are put off by the &quot;we're the true secret masters!&quot; theme and the &quot;hidden underlying truth&quot; thematic. Some of that is unavoidable - you see similar resistance to the core theme of Solars, after all core splat or no, and you can't tone it down if it's what they are and what makes them fun to play - but it's a reason to try and use the chapter fiction to smooth over this and show ways that Sidereals can be worked into games. &quot;Here's a Sidereal being better than everyone!&quot; isn't a good way to accomplish that. (Just like, say, you don't want the intro Solar fiction to portray Gaston, because you'd be playing up the problems people already have with them. Note that the Solar intro fiction is low-key and has them screwing up in several ways; the Solar survives but partially because of outside intervention, and is pretty clearly endangered by the Wyld Hunt.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I loved the 3e intro fiction. Apart from some confusion about what was even going on right at the end, it was super well written and didn\u2019t make anyone out to be just some chump. If you had told me before that the 3e intro fiction was a freshly exalted dawn being ambushed by two DBs and a Sidereal and getting away I\u2019d have rolled my eyes and said \u201cwell here we go again.\u201d But it\u2019s not like that at all. I think it actually does a way better job of making terrestrials AND Solars AND Sidereals out to be both heroes and villains alike than the DB fiction.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re right about not making other splats look bad for the sake of making Sidereals look good, but there must be some way to give them some sort of concrete \u201cthis is what happens when the Sidereals do their jobs.\u201d Rather than just being mysterious and in the background. Being agents of heaven they risk being portrayed as the real heroes who actually know what\u2019s going on and everyone else is their pawn, but I\u2019d argue not more than Solars risk being portrayed as the only real heroes with the power to do anything and everyone else is their backup dancer.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe downplay the corruption and infighting and play up how there\u2019s just too few resources and not enough credible info to go around. Make something where there\u2019s almost an x-files style shadow war with good guy Sidereal Smoking Man And DB Mulder and Scully. <br /> <br /> I dunno that\u2019s probably too hidden even for Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 08-17-2018, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T13:02:07-07:00","id":1247135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247119#post1247119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So like:<br /> <br /> Gold - there's a 60% chance of the solars continuing being huge assholes, a 35% chance of them destroying the entire world, killing everyone, and a 5% chance of everything getting so much better<br /> Bronze- There's a 100% chance that the solars won't destroy the world. The DBs will take over and it won't be as good, but things will keep running<br /> <br /> Chejop - &quot;Let's go with the Solars not murdering everyone and destroying everything, yeah?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, with the phrasing present in the core book, I like to imagine it playing out as them prognosticating a number of scenarios, some of which extended from trying to fix up the Solars, and others based on overthrowing and sealing them away. The results from the former were many and varied, and of the latter were unpalatable but consistent.<br /> <br /> I think there's something to be said for the game leaning too heavily on stacking the deck against the Vision of Gold, in a way that kind of presents a mixed message about it; everybody is supposed to agree that it's an outside chance, with some areas inferring that going for the outside chance with the better result is the more heroic option, but the chance is <i>so</i> outside that it also kind of makes it look like an irresponsible gamble.<br /> <br /> For the moment, I'm attached to the idea that the visions supporting the Solars weren't really something quantifiable, and that the odds weren't <i>that</i> terrible, but between enough of those scenarios ending in failure and maybe some of the details that they saw in particular outcomes, many of them were extremely antsy about that side of things. That Chejop and his supporters were able to argue that it was too important to take a gamble on, even though the alternative was fairly reasonable.<br /> <br /> But otherwise, yes, I think it would be better for the Bronze side to phrase the diminished world as the price for being rid of the Solars, rather than something guaranteed forever.<br /> <br /> Hell, framing it like that actually suggests the possibility that the world could have eventually gotten <i>better</i>, even without the Solars. I'm not super invested in the splat war, but I think it's okay to lean a bit away from a diminished world being the best that one can get with the Dragon Blooded, even with their disadvantages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T13:09:01-07:00","id":1247138,"title":"","content":"Honestly the chances for even have to be that bad to be irresponsible. If there was even a 50% chance to make the Solars see the error of their ways and stopping the descent into madness, but the attempt would mean they blow their only shot to usurp them, that\u2019s not great. Risk the whole world on a coin flip, no thanks. Then again killing almost all your friends and people you advise might have factored into it, it\u2019s not like Sidereals don\u2019t have emotions, so it could it was probably less than 50%.<br /> <br /> edited for atrocious spelling errors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 08-17-2018, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T14:45:04-07:00","id":1247173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247116#post1247116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it's all right for Sidereal prophecy to be fallible, but I think that, even with the Great Curse, there's an issue with the idea that they're widely unaware of a blindspot regarding things like the Underworld or Wyld.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I feel as though prophecies around the Usurpation should have been fairly focused on the subject of the Solars, rather than making promises about the distant future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. I think that the underlying presentation of the Fair Folk invasion and the Great Contagion as the Sidereals' great failure is unavoidable, though. There's more to the Usurpation than the Great Prophecy and the Usurpation itself - there's a core philosophy to the Bronze Faction that IMHO the books ought to go into more detail on.<br /> <br /> They believe that the ideal state of the world is essentially the best and the brightest Sidereals ruling the world from behind the scenes, using other Exalted as puppet kings. Whether the Great Prophecy encompassed those exact details isn't really relevant, because the core of Kejak Chejop's philosophy is essentially that only he (and the Sidereals) can be trusted to do what is necessary and that they were therefore justified in seizing control.<br /> <br /> In other words, rather than viewing the madness of the Solars, the Great Prophecy and the Usurpation as the big philosophical center of the Bronze Faction, I feel it's better to view them as the precipitating event that catalyzed a larger, more all-encompassing philosophy of Sidereal leadership.<br /> <br /> In particular, this explains the Sidereal attitude towards Lunars - yes, the Lunars are buttmad, but I don't feel it's credible for the game to try and argue that the failure to make peace with them for 1500 years is entirely on the Lunars. There needs to be some deeper political or philosophical disagreement for that to make sense, and the reality that the Bronze Faction would never, ever, ever accept anything remotely approximating equal power-sharing with the Lunars - and the Lunars are aware of this - explains a great deal. It's not necessarily as clear-cut as the Bronze Faction intentionally choosing war - they're not idiots - but the Usurpation was more than just a decision to kill the Solars; it was a decision to place absolute faith in Sidereal judgement and Sidereal prophecy, with all other Exalted rising or falling according to this. I feel the Bronze Faction is willing to kill and die for this... and I feel that what the Great Contagion and the Fair Folk invasion reveal is that (while they would never put it this way, since they feel that this principle is necessary for Creation's survival), they are willing to risk Creation itself.<br /> <br /> If the Sidereals had managed to make peace with the Lunars during the Shogunate, for instance, it is unlikely that the Fair Folk invasion would have succeeded, and it's possible even the Contagion could have been limited by their combined force. Huge amounts of energy and resources and time was wasted on that conflict. And I think the Sidereals thought they were genuinely making the right choice! They'd say that the Lunars were too dangerous, too unpredictable, too driven by their short-sighted rage or whatever, and that's not <i>entirely</i> wrong. But what the Sidereals failed to see was that they themselves were dangerous and unpredictable and driven by emotion as well. The conflict with the Lunars was at least <i>partially</i> a result of Sidereal intransigence.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it more simply, the severity of the damage done by the Great Contagion and the Fair Folk invasion is at least partially the fault of the Sidereals (it has to be, since they were in charge at the time), but the really serious problem isn't the Usurpation, it's their mismanagement in the ~750 years afterwards. Even presuming the Solars had to die, Creation could have been a lot more ready for those shocks than it was.<br /> <br /> Obviously the Lunars and the Dragon-Blooded also share some blame. Everyone screwed up at one point or another. I mean if you go back far enough it's the fault of the Solars for succumbing to madness and bringing things to that point, too. But my point is that it's more useful to look at it as a fundamental failure of the entire Bronze Faction philosophy, rather than a specific mechanical screw-up with their Fate powers or whatever. The Bronze Faction didn't just murder the Solars (which the prophecy said was necessary), they intentionally weakened the Dragon-Blooded and suppressed the Lunars, and as a result, when Creation faced a threat that was less suitable to being confronted by Sidereal power alone, it folded.<br /> <br /> It's not that they were unaware of the holes in their capabilities. They knew perfectly well. They chose to gamble that their power, combined with the diminished Dragon-Blooded, could protect Creation from anything unexpected that wandered in from outside its boundaries. And for 700 years they were right, so it wasn't a <i>totally</i> bad bet. But I feel that it wasn't entirely driven by reason and cold calculation, either, whatever Kejak might try to argue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 08-17-2018, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T14:58:44-07:00","id":1247180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247173#post1247173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, to put it more simply, the severity of the damage done by the Great Contagion and the Fair Folk invasion is at least partially the fault of the Sidereals (it has to be, since they were in charge at the time), but the really serious problem isn't the Usurpation, it's their mismanagement in the ~750 years afterwards. Even presuming the Solars had to die, Creation could have been a lot more ready for those shocks than it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>THis is where we will inherently disagree. Both of those things are no ones fault. Even if they could see it coming, these were both essentially two apocalyptic events that we don't even know if the first age could have wiped out. The solar charmset is impressive but without charms that currently don't exist, they are unable to treat the masses. They'd probably handle it a lot better than sidereals could but these events are so out of anyone's hands it's impossible to blame one group for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T15:27:42-07:00","id":1247188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247180#post1247180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THis is where we will inherently disagree. Both of those things are no ones fault.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem very thematically consistent to have a long period of sharp decline that has nothing whatsoever to do with the enormous disaster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if they could see it coming, these were both essentially two apocalyptic events that we don't even know if the first age could have wiped out. The solar charmset is impressive but without charms that currently don't exist, they are unable to treat the masses. They'd probably handle it a lot better than sidereals could</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to use the Sword of Creation without having to jump through a lot of hoops first would have helped a lot there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T15:45:20-07:00","id":1247193,"title":"","content":"I think a big thing to consider in evaluating the Contagion as something the Prophecy can account for or not, is whether the Prophecy was an actual choice, or whether it was a false-choice that the Bronze stumbled into and picked the wrong answer.<br /> <br /> Contagion as something the Prophecy can account for means that in the end, you ahve to weigh the world we have with the world that could have been, but it still makes things ultimately something Sidereals had a choice on. While a Contagoin independent of the Prophecy and such means that there was no choice, Sidereals were just objectively wrong and the Vision fo Gold wa sthe right one. Or it is implied. Note, this is actually the vibe I got from a lot of the gamleine itself in 2e and from many people thorugh the years since 1e.<br /> <br /> I think giving Sidereals enough agency to account for that, makes for a better story in the end. And that hte Contagion could have been mitigated or ecovered through better in cotnext of the Bronze's actions is probably a better story for moral dilema, not giving objective &quot;Sidereals are wrong, Solar reign is always the right asnwer&quot;, and something that I think is better for games that do assume you might be able to play one of these guys and not make it so that one part of the group is Objectivley Wrong.<br /> <br /> I'll also agree that depending on how 3e goes, the Contaigon probably would of still been apocalyptic and caused havoic and destruction of society. Though note that baed on the history in Arms, Creation has had a few of those, and it's not really clear the era labeled Dreams of the First Age would have survived it even if the Gold managed to work. For all we know, it's he even to setup the total destruction to fulfil its othe rparts. THat's the big issue with &quot;might ahve beens&quot; and all that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T15:54:12-07:00","id":1247198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247188#post1247188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't seem very thematically consistent to have a long period of sharp decline that has nothing whatsoever to do with the enormous disaster.<br /> <br /> Being able to use the Sword of Creation without having to jump through a lot of hoops first would have helped a lot there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that solars have less hoops to jump through but we don't know who had control of it. It's possible those Solars died first leaving a similar situation in place. There are too many what ifs to say that both events are a direct result of the usurpation rather than a situation which was unavoidable in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T16:37:43-07:00","id":1247220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247066#post1247066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both the Fair Folk and the Underworld (which was the origin of the Great Contagion) are outside of fate's purview. Creation survived that because of luck or, if you prefer, because that's just the way things happened, like in the real world. But it wasn't preserved by any sort of fate. That was literally the entire reason that &quot;outside of fate&quot; was created as a category. And there's important reasons it was set up that way...</div> </div> </div> </div>I desire to fill a cup with water. I cannot move the faucet. I can move the cup. Woe to me for I cannot move the faucet, for it is beyond my reach, unlike the cup, which I can affect. If only I could do something with the cup, that is not beyond my reach, to ensure the faucet is positioned over it to fill it with water. But woe, it is not possible for me, who can move the cup, to ensure the faucet fills it, because I cannot move the faucet. If only there were some way that I, who can leverage motion upon the cup, could ensure the faucet I cannot move would fill it with water. But this is an unsolvable conundrum. Alas and alack!<br /> <br /> Also, ordinary raksha and demons below the Third Circle, and ghosts without comparable strength become entangled in fate when they're within its' boundaries, so unless the Great Contagion was secretly a Third Circle Demon-equivalent spirit, and the Balorian Crusade was composed entirely of Unshaped, they become predictable by the RAW we know.<br /> <br /> If my giving the cup incentive to move towards underneath the faucet denies it protagonism then so too do storytellers by setting up conditions which heroic characters respond to, hopefully in a manner they expect - sure, maybe the PC will join in beating the slave rather than stop the slaver, but I think characters tend to be a little more predictable than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-17-2018, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T16:49:35-07:00","id":1247225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247198#post1247198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's true that solars have less hoops to jump through but we don't know who had control of it. It's possible those Solars died first leaving a similar situation in place. There are too many what ifs to say that both events are a direct result of the usurpation rather than a situation which was unavoidable in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the setting a thing that exists, or a narrative for the sake of being compelling and conveying theme?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T17:01:02-07:00","id":1247229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247225#post1247225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the setting a thing that exists, or a narrative for the sake of being compelling and conveying theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>That theme would make sense if it were directly the sidereal's fault that this event happened. However, even solars would have a hard time dealing with this and caught by surprise it would have killed the less hardy of them. We're dealing with a situation no one would have seen coming or could have seen coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T18:07:54-07:00","id":1247250,"title":"","content":"Before I would address anything said specifically again, I want to briefly bring up a point that I forgot about when it came up earlier: the sense that the idea of things being Outside Fate (at least as regards being an obstacle to the foresight of Sidereals, or the viability of their long term plans) has shown itself a bit to not be the best thing in practice. Partially because of the degree to which it seems to undermine the credibility of the Sidereals in the eyes of many readers, partially because its actual mechanical implementation always seemed kind of spotty (neither previous Edition gave it anything to do with actual prophetic Charms), and partially because predicting some horrible monster from the Wyld or Hell seems like precisely the kind of thing that Sidereals should be doing.<br /> <br /> When I said that it's okay for Sidereal prophecy to be fallible, that was partially a sense of their being latitude for circumstances or choices to shift things away from what a Sidereal predicted, and partially based on the weird and circuitous ways that those Charms were written. One might combine that with a sense that the Sidereals themselves can be fallible in the form of not always asking the right questions (the return of the Solars catching them off guard can really be as simple as nobody ever asking if that was going to come up in the next few years), and an idea that some of their prophecy has always been a bit of a cheat in the form of them predicting something that they themselves have Fated to happen (with at least some fault in <i>that</i> being something they definitely can't do to demons or behemoths from Zen-Mu).<br /> <br /> Otherwise I feel as though a straightforward idea of some of the major parts of the setting being simply invisible to an important part of the Sidereals' toolset kind of sells them short.<br /> <br /> This all arose from a sense that at least one way in which the First Age could deal with a gigantic fae crusade led by a Raksha Incarna was authorities of the Realm being warned by a prophecy from Heaven.<br /> <br /> Mind, even if they were facing something at full strength, I would assume that many parts of the First Age were vastly better suited to dealing with it than the tail end of the Shogunate. Good Lord, what else are those royal warstriders that you've been churning out daiklaves to get the white points to create even good for, if not working in concert to cancel the apocalypse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T23:21:44-07:00","id":1247293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247220#post1247220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, ordinary raksha and demons below the Third Circle, and ghosts without comparable strength become entangled in fate when they're within its' boundaries, so unless the Great Contagion was secretly a Third Circle Demon-equivalent spirit, and the Balorian Crusade was composed entirely of Unshaped, they become predictable by the RAW we know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deathlords are on par with Third Circle Demons, and they created the Great Contagion in the Underworld. So Fate wouldn't have mattered until the disease was released into Creation. Considering how lethal it was, and fast it spread, it was already to late by the time the Sidereals became aware of it. Also, it was the Unshaped that planned the Balorean Crusade. They brought a massive force with them from beyond Creation's borders. So again, by the time they entered Creation and became tangled in Fate, it was to late for the Sidereals to do anything other then react to the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T01:43:52-07:00","id":1247308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247293#post1247293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Deathlords are on par with Third Circle Demons, and they created the Great Contagion in the Underworld. So Fate wouldn't have mattered until the disease was released into Creation. Considering how lethal it was, and fast it spread, it was already to late by the time the Sidereals became aware of it. Also, it was the Unshaped that planned the Balorean Crusade. They brought a massive force with them from beyond Creation's borders. So again, by the time they entered Creation and became tangled in Fate, it was to late for the Sidereals to do anything other then react to the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the great contagion was pulled from the well of urd?<br /> <br /> I also thought the Ishvara who are shaped planned the invasion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T02:33:38-07:00","id":1247317,"title":"","content":"It's a bit over the top, but I actually still retain a soft spot for the idea that observing the Great Contagion through magic based on the Loom was a vector of infection.<br /> <br /> \u2026 That was in an actual book, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T03:19:00-07:00","id":1247323,"title":"","content":"I don't remember it anywhere, but it's possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T03:52:07-07:00","id":1247331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247323#post1247323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember it anywhere, but it's possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that it's something that I would have gotten in those heady early days of entry into Exalted discussion, prior to actually owning a single book, when a lot of ideas were being thrown around and there was no firm basis for telling what was and was not published. Heck, if it wasn't ever in a book, I would imagine that the person that I first read it from got it second or third-hand, and thought themselves that it was.<br /> <br /> That said, my mind is conjuring an image of seeing something along those lines in a book (although that could easily be a fabrication).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T04:17:07-07:00","id":1247339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247173#post1247173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda. I think that the underlying presentation of the Fair Folk invasion and the Great Contagion as the Sidereals' great failure is unavoidable, though. There's more to the Usurpation than the Great Prophecy and the Usurpation itself - there's a core philosophy to the Bronze Faction that IMHO the books ought to go into more detail on.<br /> <br /> They believe that the ideal state of the world is essentially the best and the brightest Sidereals ruling the world from behind the scenes, using other Exalted as puppet kings. Whether the Great Prophecy encompassed those exact details isn't really relevant, because the core of Kejak Chejop's philosophy is essentially that only he (and the Sidereals) can be trusted to do what is necessary and that they were therefore justified in seizing control.<br /> <br /> In other words, rather than viewing the madness of the Solars, the Great Prophecy and the Usurpation as the big philosophical center of the Bronze Faction, I feel it's better to view them as the precipitating event that catalyzed a larger, more all-encompassing philosophy of Sidereal leadership.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be a response to the argument in this post in full (which way too much being argued than I have time to get into and also I don't really want to distract from the broader and more interesting arguments currently dominating this thread!), but generally just on this point, I would qualify all of the above that by about mid-1e it was established that there are a number of constraints on why the Sidereals might chose to rule in secret, when they would feel that there is no alternative but to take on much of the role in running the world:<br /> <br /> 1) The breaking of the Mask: Depicted in 1e as an accidental effect of overshooting the preparations for the Usurpation.<br /> 2) The canon is that Solars openly ceased to disregard their advice, telling them to &quot;butt out&quot; effectively, and the Lunars of the First Age were in close alliance with the Solars, leaving few options for partnership. The first mover here, against a dialogue, is the Solar Exalted and clearly the Solar Exalted. (To the degree the canon is clear, it's clear that the Sidereals fit within the system as advisors and the Solars disdained the relationship, not that Sidereals were first movers in developing an ideology that they should rule). That's gotta constrain the degree to which the Sidereals had to operate a closed shop.<br /> 3) Their integration into the First Age world government and Heaven, where they were expected to be unobtrusive, of the Heavens, and absent from human civilization for the most part, and that seems to be the role that the Five Maidens wanted them to have; virtually akin to the role that the gods held (Yu Shan governed largely for and by the gods, Creation for the mortals), and maintained for the same reasons that division was maintained (albeit that the Sidereals are limnal figures). Indeed if this were not the case, and they left a high density of traces within the world, it would be hard to sustain.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are members among them that do believe they should be in charge with no voice for anyone else, for purely ideological reasons, but I think no more frequent than among the other Celestials (and perhaps less so if you compare to the Solars of the First Age zenith).<br /> <br /> Not that I guess you couldn't go back to the 1e core and go &quot;But all the above are just set dressing on their true preference!&quot;. I think that would be to discard a more interesting articulated set of circumstances that led them to where they are, though.<br /> <br /> As a coda, just because I don't think it would be right to wholly ignore the overall thesis of your post, I generally (and no surprise) disagree. But it's interesting that systematic Sidereal dysfunction, and this being because they chose to exclude other contributors is arguable, even if I think it's mostly wrong, and I would not necessarily want to totally squash that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T04:51:33-07:00","id":1247348,"title":"","content":"I would not be surprised if the &quot;contagious through even Fate&quot; were to be somewhere in a book, probably 2e with its characteristic &quot;also, fuck Sidereals&quot; aplomb.<br /> <br /> Funny, I was just thinking there needs to be more evidence of Sidereals left in Creation. As it stands, it seems like it wants to do the Men in Black thing of &quot;we're responsible for stopping a hundred apocalypses you have never heard of&quot; as what makes them exciting and compelling, but then we never see any of it, so all we see is &quot;they didn't see it coming&quot; and &quot;they made a guy choke but not die on fish bones (IMPORTANT: NOT CHICKEN)&quot; which... Paints a far less compelling image.<br /> <br /> I realize this is intentional in character - arcane fate, evidence lost, memories lost, etc etc etc - but the problem is this has an out of character impact. There is little to point to and say &quot;this is what Sidereals do&quot; except for this general sense of &quot;the Creation that until I told you it was maintained by Sidereals you would have thought was entirely self maintaining, is kept in order by them&quot;... And so we get this sense of Sidereal impotence and ineptitude being somehow the correct and proper state of affairs. Which is a pretty sad state of affairs for an entire exalt type. <br /> <br /> I dunno. I guess I feel like it's a thing that could use a tweak in the new edition. Some things just being too big to be swept under the rug, so they instead become local legend, details lost or exaggerated to explain why the nearby giant statue has an arm perfectly sheared off or the river meanders and flows in all the wrong ways.<br /> <br /> As a friend of mine said, &quot;they can do the Men in Black thing but they need to show the Noisy Cricket fired once or twice.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-18-2018, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T07:21:36-07:00","id":1247374,"title":"","content":"I find Exalted: The Sidereals isn't too bad at telling you in general terms, who they are and what they do, why they matter to human history, and the active, choice based actions they take to hold human cultures together. It does not over-emphasize, to my mind, that they just maintain the fabric of reality in a holding pattern or do random tasks they don't understand for ends they don't know.<br /> <br /> The problems we might have as a fan community in talking about this are probably due to;<br /> <br /> a) We never had Caste books for the Sidereals, so actually fleshing out with individual cases and specific examples, is a bit thin on the ground. Adventures and campaigns also weren't written for Sidereal perspectives, so it's lacking a bit there as well. The only real material about what they do is in the two Sidereal books, and MoEP:Sidereals is widely thought to be a fairly poor book.<br /> <br /> b) There was a fashion about in the fan community during 2e to think it was better (&quot;edgier&quot; I guess you could say) to have the Sidereals be indifferent to human culture and human welfare and simply be concerned with maintaining reality and existence as a whole. As well as to amp up the elements of &quot;Sidereals have random missions they don't understand to generate butterflies moving Creation onto the right course&quot; and of course, &quot;Creation has only experienced decline at all scales during the Age of Sorrows&quot; (rather than emphasize the Age of Sorrows as a time of rebuilding and new things as well).<br /> <br /> I could speculate about why this happened, but ultimately probably mostly as everyone was caught up in the trend and there weren't any authoritative, respected, charismatic voices to actually go back, look at what was written, be willing to argue for that and push back on what was popular, sadly. And we just haven't had much publishing on Sidereals since then, so the ideas have sort of stuck around and not been much displaced even if people have been writing posts against these sort of ideas since at least the beginning of 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T08:58:41-07:00","id":1247400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244941-are-the-dragon-blooded-the-good-guys?p=1247308#post1247308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the great contagion was pulled from the well of urd?<br /> <br /> I also thought the Ishvara who are shaped planned the invasion?</div> </div> </div> </div>So for 3e, neither is known. Stuff to keep in mind in context:<br /> <br /> 1) The Deathlords are being heavily changed. The source of the Contagion might be different, or at least it's implementaiton as well. Well of Udr is cool so I don't doubt it sticks around, but I expect with how the Deathlords are going to be presented in more useful game contexts, the Dowager is probably going to be presented as to ahving more than staring in to her well.<br /> <br /> 2) There are no such thing anymore as Unshaped, which is important. Balor was an Ishvara in 2e and in the textbox in the original 3e corebook draft about Ishvara as one. Whether Ishvara remains canon is to b eseen, but it's notable that these are th ethings that happen like...once an Age if that. Worrying about the next Prince Balor is like us on Earth worrying about the next Great Dying. There probably wasn't volcanic activity like that for like half a billion years to that point and I don't think we have to worry about it again anytime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}